WEBVTT

00:04.670 --> 00:08.672
(overlapping voices
speaking foreign languages)

00:08.674 --> 00:11.477
(female reporter):
The chilling announcement
was made earlier today

00:11.479 --> 00:13.380
by the Secretary
General of the UN,

00:13.382 --> 00:15.712
who was overseeing the meetings
held by world leaders

00:15.714 --> 00:18.121
at their Emergency Summit
in Athens.

00:18.123 --> 00:20.321
(male politician):
While we every day bear witness

00:20.323 --> 00:22.389
to the catastrophic
ecological collapse

00:22.391 --> 00:26.129
that is plaguing our planet,
we must not forget that this is,

00:26.131 --> 00:28.032
above all, a human crisis.

00:28.601 --> 00:30.628
The sudden
and devastating scarcity

00:30.630 --> 00:32.531
of food, water and resources,

00:32.533 --> 00:35.435
once only an issue
for our most vulnerable,

00:35.437 --> 00:37.437
now spares no one,

00:37.439 --> 00:41.111
and it requires a response
like none before.

00:41.113 --> 00:43.344
(female reporter):
He went on to add
that starting tomorrow,

00:43.346 --> 00:46.215
all international
borders will be closed,

00:46.217 --> 00:47.876
and every nation
will have one year

00:47.878 --> 00:50.483
to meet their population
reduction goals.

00:53.653 --> 00:56.192
(♪ We're Here for a Good Time ♪
by Troopers)

01:07.832 --> 01:10.074
♪ A very good friend of mine ♪

01:11.110 --> 01:13.737
♪ Told me something
the other day ♪

01:15.642 --> 01:18.511
♪ I'd like to pass on to you ♪

01:18.513 --> 01:20.777
♪ 'Cause I believe what
he said to be true ♪

01:22.715 --> 01:25.716
♪ He said
we're here for a good time ♪

01:27.423 --> 01:29.918
♪ Not a long time ♪

01:29.920 --> 01:31.557
♪ Not a long time ♪

01:32.026 --> 01:33.889
♪ So have a good time ♪

01:33.891 --> 01:36.694
♪ The sun can't shine
every day ♪

01:38.665 --> 01:41.204
♪ And the sun is shinin' ♪

01:42.603 --> 01:44.999
♪ In this rainy city ♪

01:46.442 --> 01:49.036
♪ And the sun is shinin' ♪

01:49.742 --> 01:53.348
♪ Ooh, isn't it a pity ♪

01:55.517 --> 01:59.321
♪ And every year
has its share of tears ♪

01:59.623 --> 02:02.588
♪ Every now and then
it's gotta rain ♪

02:02.590 --> 02:04.821
♪ We're here for a good time ♪

02:06.726 --> 02:08.924
♪ Not a long time ♪

02:11.060 --> 02:13.335
♪ So have a good time ♪

02:13.337 --> 02:16.206
♪ The sun can't shine
every day ♪

02:33.786 --> 02:36.292
♪ And the sun is shinin' ♪

02:37.394 --> 02:40.120
♪ In this rainy city ♪

02:41.662 --> 02:44.267
♪ And the sun is shinin' ♪

02:44.669 --> 02:48.337
♪ Ooh, isn't it a pity ♪

02:50.902 --> 02:54.673
♪ And every year
has its share of tears ♪

02:55.108 --> 02:58.006
♪ Every now and then
it's gotta rain ♪

02:58.008 --> 03:00.140
♪ We're here for a good time ♪

03:02.012 --> 03:04.353
♪ Not a long time ♪

03:06.522 --> 03:08.786
♪ So have a good time ♪

03:08.788 --> 03:11.954
♪ The sun can't shine
every day ♪

03:11.956 --> 03:13.461
♪ Shine every day ♪

03:13.763 --> 03:15.958
♪ We're here for a good time ♪

03:15.960 --> 03:18.125
♪ We're here for a good time ♪

03:18.127 --> 03:19.863
♪ Not a long time ♪

03:19.865 --> 03:22.404
♪ Not a long time ♪

03:22.406 --> 03:25.242
♪ So have a good time
Have a good time ♪

03:25.244 --> 03:27.035
♪ The sun can't shine
every day ♪

03:27.037 --> 03:28.872
♪ The sun can't shine
every day ♪♪

03:29.140 --> 03:30.709
(car stereo stops)

03:30.711 --> 03:33.415
(crickets chirping)

03:40.886 --> 03:44.052
(political commentator):
<i> Come on, Professor, are you</i>
<i> seriously telling our viewers</i>

03:44.054 --> 03:45.988
<i> that you are in favour</i>
<i> of conscription?</i>

03:45.990 --> 03:48.155
(Jared):<i> I am in favour</i>
<i> of this government</i>

03:48.157 --> 03:50.564
<i> doing whatever it takes</i>
<i> to win this war.</i>

03:50.566 --> 03:51.829
(political commentator):
<i> Please stop referring</i>

03:51.831 --> 03:53.897
<i> to this crisis as a war.</i>
<i> It's not a war.</i>

03:53.899 --> 03:55.734
<i> Wars have opposing sides.</i>

03:55.736 --> 03:58.341
(Jared):
<i> Humanity is the opposing side.</i>

03:58.343 --> 04:01.542
<i> We are engaged in nothing less</i>
<i> than a life and death struggle</i>

04:01.544 --> 04:03.203
<i> against our own extinction.</i>

04:03.205 --> 04:04.644
(political commentator):
<i> Unbelievable.</i>

04:04.646 --> 04:06.382
<i> So what else are you all for?</i>

04:06.384 --> 04:09.077
<i> How about lowering</i>
<i> the age of eligibility?</i>

04:09.079 --> 04:10.210
(Jared):<i> Why not?</i>

04:10.212 --> 04:11.354
<i> Plenty of individuals</i>

04:11.356 --> 04:12.982
<i> under the age of 18</i>

04:12.984 --> 04:14.214
<i> have expressed a desire,</i>

04:14.216 --> 04:16.326
<i> a willingness, to enlist.</i>

04:16.328 --> 04:18.526
<i> I see no reason</i>

04:18.528 --> 04:20.858
<i> why we shouldn't at least</i>
<i> consider their wishes.</i>

04:20.860 --> 04:23.366
(political commentator):
<i> Consider the wishes</i>
<i> of children?</i>

04:23.368 --> 04:25.126
(Jared):
<i> I didn't say "children."</i>

04:25.128 --> 04:27.568
<i> But I do have</i>
<i> a 10-year-old son myself.</i>

04:27.570 --> 04:30.538
<i> 10? Are you saying</i>
<i> that this administration</i>

04:30.540 --> 04:32.133
<i> is considering letting</i>
<i> 10-year-olds enlist?</i>

04:32.135 --> 04:34.905
<i>Professor York I sincerely hope</i>
<i>your son is not watching today.</i>

04:34.907 --> 04:36.511
(Jared):
<i> I sincerely hope he is.</i>

04:36.513 --> 04:38.348
<i> He needs to know exactly</i>
<i> what's at stake.</i>

04:38.350 --> 04:39.910
<i> Every nation on this planet</i>

04:39.912 --> 04:41.384
<i> needs to honour</i>
<i> their commitments</i>

04:41.386 --> 04:43.782
<i> to the Athens Accord,</i>

04:43.784 --> 04:46.818
<i> and we are severely</i>
<i> behind our 20% pledge.</i>

04:46.820 --> 04:48.688
<i> Not enough people</i>
<i> are willing to enlist!</i>

04:48.690 --> 04:50.525
(slams fist)
Fuck that guy!

04:50.527 --> 04:52.285
I don't see him signing up.

04:52.287 --> 04:54.089
(Jared):
<i> ...our government come up</i>

04:54.091 --> 04:56.223
<i> with its initial enlistment</i>
<i> estimates. Okay?</i>

04:56.225 --> 04:58.258
I am sorry, Mr. York.

04:58.260 --> 04:59.930
(Jared):<i> I made the mistake</i>
<i> of assuming...</i>

04:59.932 --> 05:01.602
(Charles):
No apology needed.

05:02.037 --> 05:04.066
(Jared):<i> ...selfless enough</i>
<i> to willingly enlist.</i>

05:04.068 --> 05:05.408
I agree.

05:05.410 --> 05:06.607
(Jared):
<i> ...to volunteer.</i>

05:06.609 --> 05:08.345
<i> Turns out people</i>
<i> are far more selfish</i>

05:08.347 --> 05:09.841
<i> than I believed they were.</i>

05:10.910 --> 05:13.141
(eerie music)

05:52.622 --> 05:54.457
(TV reporter):
<i> ...the fallout continues</i>

05:54.459 --> 05:56.151
<i> over the Kremlin's</i>
<i> announcement last week</i>

05:56.153 --> 05:58.021
<i> that Russia has satisfied</i>
<i> their commitment</i>

05:58.023 --> 05:59.825
<i> to the Athens Accord</i>

05:59.827 --> 06:01.629
<i> three months</i>
<i> ahead of the UN deadline.</i>

06:01.631 --> 06:04.027
Oh, you're already working
on the mackerel?

06:04.029 --> 06:07.096
It must be wonderful to be
handling fresh seafood again.

06:08.473 --> 06:11.903
This is the hardest thing
I've ever done in my life.

06:12.472 --> 06:16.611
And I'm including my years
as a war correspondent.

06:20.342 --> 06:22.914
The piano looks so strange
in the bedroom.

06:23.521 --> 06:25.015
But you were right.

06:25.017 --> 06:26.115
It fits.

06:28.020 --> 06:29.954
Want to come up
and see for yourself?

06:29.956 --> 06:31.593
There's still time
before the kids arrive.

06:34.026 --> 06:35.861
Oh, Dawn.

06:37.029 --> 06:38.435
I'm sorry.

06:40.362 --> 06:42.197
You said you wanted to cook.

06:43.805 --> 06:45.068
I'll go.

06:47.336 --> 06:49.413
(Dawn sobs quietly)

06:50.515 --> 06:52.108
Oh, honey. Come.

06:52.110 --> 06:53.516
(TV reporter):
<i> "...this is fake news.</i>

06:53.518 --> 06:55.078
<i> We are not a branch</i>
<i> of the military.</i>

06:55.080 --> 06:57.784
<i> We're a department made up</i>
<i> of compassionate individuals</i>

06:57.786 --> 07:01.524
<i>dedicated to helping our nation</i>
<i> in its greatest hour of need."</i>

07:01.526 --> 07:03.251
<i> Coming up after the break,</i>

07:03.253 --> 07:05.121
<i> we'll bring you more</i>
<i> on the York Therapeutics</i>

07:05.123 --> 07:06.188
<i> class-action trial.</i>

07:06.190 --> 07:08.531
<i> The courtroom erupted today</i>

07:08.533 --> 07:10.929
<i> when one of the plaintiffs</i>
<i> confronted CEO Rachel York,</i>

07:10.931 --> 07:14.394
<i>blaming Ms. York personally for</i>
<i> her debilitating chronic pain.</i>

07:15.001 --> 07:16.935
(tires squeal)

07:16.937 --> 07:18.970
(engine revs)

07:20.173 --> 07:22.941
(female computer voice):
<i> Exterior UV levels</i>
<i> are moderate.</i>

07:22.943 --> 07:25.075
<i> Proceed with caution.</i>

07:25.517 --> 07:27.110
(phone rings)

07:27.512 --> 07:30.080
-Hello?
-(Beth):<i> What the fuck is</i>
<i> the matter with you?!</i>

07:30.082 --> 07:32.753
<i> You go on TV and you tell your</i>
<i>son that he should kill himself?</i>

07:32.755 --> 07:34.249
That's not what I said, Beth.

07:34.251 --> 07:35.921
I didn't say he should
kill himself.

07:35.923 --> 07:37.725
That reporter fucking
twisted my words.

07:37.727 --> 07:39.958
(Beth):<i> No, no, no. Don't blame</i>
<i> the interviewer, Jared.</i>

07:39.960 --> 07:42.763
<i> Okay? You said what you said,</i>
<i> and now Lucas is...</i>

07:42.765 --> 07:44.094
<i> is bawling his eyes out.</i>

07:44.096 --> 07:45.425
Um, okay.

07:45.427 --> 07:46.932
Um... can I just speak to him?

07:46.934 --> 07:48.769
Would you mind putting
him on the phone?

07:48.771 --> 07:49.737
I'd love to chat with him.

07:49.739 --> 07:51.134
(Beth):
<i> No! Not a chance!</i>

07:51.136 --> 07:52.300
<i> Are you kidding me?</i>

07:52.302 --> 07:54.071
<i>He doesn't want to speak to you.</i>

07:54.073 --> 07:55.611
Can I just come by later?

07:55.846 --> 07:57.580
I'll be gone before curfew.

07:57.582 --> 08:00.176
(Beth):
<i> No. No, you can't come by.</i>

08:00.411 --> 08:01.914
I swear to God, Beth,

08:01.916 --> 08:03.443
I didn't say our son
should enlist.

08:03.445 --> 08:05.148
(phone beeps off)

08:06.316 --> 08:08.052
(helicopter overhead)

08:08.659 --> 08:10.560
Fuck my life.

08:17.932 --> 08:19.393
Oh!

08:19.628 --> 08:21.538
What?

08:21.940 --> 08:24.871
Dawn, most of this stuff
is prohibited.

08:25.808 --> 08:27.335
Where'd you get it?

08:28.272 --> 08:29.876
(speaking Korean)

08:42.627 --> 08:44.418
(Jared):
Oh, for God's sake.

08:44.420 --> 08:45.892
(sighs)

08:45.894 --> 08:47.564
Is Noah coming tonight
or something?

08:47.566 --> 08:48.961
(Dawn):
Of course he is.

08:48.963 --> 08:50.358
He's your brother.

08:50.360 --> 08:52.393
(Jared):
I mean, adopted.

08:52.395 --> 08:54.197
Why don't you go relax
in the living room

08:54.199 --> 08:56.100
until your father
comes downstairs?

08:56.740 --> 08:58.432
Hm?

08:58.434 --> 09:01.908
(eerie music)

09:32.501 --> 09:34.138
(Mia):
Just send me home in an Uber.

09:34.140 --> 09:35.909
I'm fine now.
They don't want me here.

09:35.911 --> 09:37.537
(Rachel):
I don't care what they want.

09:37.539 --> 09:39.077
You're staying with me.

09:39.079 --> 09:41.508
Was that grandpa's
new car in the driveway?

09:41.510 --> 09:44.544
(Rachel): No, that's your
Uncle Jared's midlife crisis.

09:44.546 --> 09:46.183
I don't think it's electric.

09:46.185 --> 09:47.514
Oh, it's not.

09:49.221 --> 09:50.220
She forced me to come.

09:50.222 --> 09:52.420
Oh, I'm sorry, sweetheart.

09:55.359 --> 09:57.766
You know I'm always
happy to see you.

09:59.594 --> 10:01.363
Mia, go ask Uncle Jared
about his car.

10:09.945 --> 10:13.078
I said this was
an adults-only evening.

10:13.751 --> 10:15.179
She shouldn't be here.

10:15.714 --> 10:17.885
Yeah, well, you didn't
see her when I got home.

10:18.821 --> 10:20.855
She saw me on the news
and she was a wreck.

10:20.857 --> 10:22.890
-I couldn't leave her.
-Poor Mia.

10:22.892 --> 10:24.892
If you don't want her here,
we're both leaving.

10:24.894 --> 10:27.092
I don't have time
for whatever this is anyway.

10:27.094 --> 10:28.764
No, no. It's okay.

10:28.766 --> 10:29.765
Stay.

10:30.427 --> 10:31.833
Please stay.

10:34.431 --> 10:35.936
Now...

10:36.738 --> 10:38.873
How are things going
with the lawsuit?

10:39.876 --> 10:41.007
(scoffs)

10:43.275 --> 10:46.078
(Rachel):
Mm! Smells good in here.

10:46.080 --> 10:49.180
(♪♪)

11:07.431 --> 11:08.496
(cell beeps)

11:08.898 --> 11:11.103
<i> Hey, what happened?</i>

11:11.105 --> 11:12.676
I can't do it.

11:13.345 --> 11:16.603
I thought that I could, but
the timing's not right and...

11:17.672 --> 11:19.144
I don't know, Grace.

11:19.146 --> 11:20.343
The last time I saw him,

11:20.345 --> 11:21.850
he wouldn't even look at me.

11:21.852 --> 11:23.478
(Grace):<i> No matter</i>
<i> what your dad has planned,</i>

11:23.480 --> 11:25.447
<i> he's not going to be upset</i>
<i> by what you have to say</i>

11:25.449 --> 11:27.020
<i>after what he just did for you.</i>

11:27.222 --> 11:30.221
I know what he did for me.

11:31.323 --> 11:33.389
But you don't know him.

11:33.657 --> 11:35.028
You've never met him!

11:35.296 --> 11:38.328
He hates surprises and I can't
just hijack his night

11:38.330 --> 11:40.165
because he'd hate that.

11:40.167 --> 11:42.970
And that's okay
because I just... I need...

11:43.272 --> 11:44.367
(Grace):<i> Noah.</i>

11:44.369 --> 11:45.665
I need more time.

11:45.667 --> 11:46.666
<i> Noah.</i>

11:47.603 --> 11:48.811
<i> Close your eyes.</i>

11:49.605 --> 11:51.341
<i> Take a deep breath.</i>

11:52.443 --> 11:54.311
<i> Picture yourself calm.</i>

11:55.514 --> 11:58.183
<i> Picture yourself in the place</i>
<i> you're most comfortable.</i>

11:58.818 --> 12:01.384
<i> Now tell me: what do you see?</i>

12:01.753 --> 12:03.320
Our apartment.

12:05.390 --> 12:06.554
You.

12:08.690 --> 12:10.129
Just you.

12:10.901 --> 12:12.296
(Grace):<i> Go home.</i>

12:12.298 --> 12:13.869
<i> I'll meet you there soon.</i>

12:13.871 --> 12:15.937
<i> We can get under the sheets</i>
<i> and watch TV.</i>

12:17.633 --> 12:20.040
-I love you.
<i> -And I love you.</i>

12:24.882 --> 12:27.014
(Ashley):
Uh-uh. Not a chance.

12:27.016 --> 12:28.609
If I'm doing this, so are you.

12:31.119 --> 12:32.712
Get in!

12:36.388 --> 12:38.091
In case you're wondering,

12:38.093 --> 12:41.226
I just had a commercial audition
for a video game.

12:41.228 --> 12:42.931
It's great. You know?

12:42.933 --> 12:44.625
Five years of theatre school

12:44.627 --> 12:47.870
and this is what my life
has come to:

12:47.872 --> 12:52.908
praying to book a commercial
for a video game.

12:53.176 --> 12:54.844
I'm sorry, Ash.

12:55.737 --> 12:56.846
Something I could do?

12:56.848 --> 12:58.738
Yeah, you could convince

12:58.740 --> 13:00.278
the 50 other girls
I'm up against

13:00.280 --> 13:01.774
to enlist.

13:01.776 --> 13:03.644
That could help me a lot.

13:03.646 --> 13:04.986
I could try.

13:05.681 --> 13:07.054
Okay. Thank you.
(laughs)

13:07.056 --> 13:09.155
-I'm pretty convincing.
-Yeah, you are.

13:09.157 --> 13:10.717
(laughs)

13:10.719 --> 13:12.455
(Noah):
Any idea why Dad invited us to--

13:12.457 --> 13:15.755
No. Uh... my guess is
he's gonna tell us

13:15.757 --> 13:17.966
that he's going back to work.

13:18.468 --> 13:20.265
Must be killing him he retired

13:20.267 --> 13:22.729
just before the story
of the century broke.

13:22.731 --> 13:25.633
And you know Dad,
it's all about his legacy.

13:25.635 --> 13:27.107
(laughs)

13:27.742 --> 13:29.637
Why did I even bother coming?

13:30.882 --> 13:32.442
Hang tight.

13:41.552 --> 13:43.156
Who's Grace?

13:43.424 --> 13:45.752
Uh...
(chuckles nervously)

13:45.754 --> 13:47.490
Nobody. Just a friend.

13:47.492 --> 13:50.834
Oh, my God, do you have
a booty call after dinner?

13:51.136 --> 13:53.837
I mean, it's not a booty call
if you live together.

13:59.108 --> 14:02.076
(sinister music)

14:07.512 --> 14:10.777
I met her, um... at a meeting.

14:11.646 --> 14:15.023
You know, she's been clean
for a long time, and...

14:16.191 --> 14:18.620
Look, I was gonna
tell Dad tonight,

14:18.622 --> 14:20.259
but it's not the time

14:20.261 --> 14:22.228
because I don't want to get
in the way of...

14:22.230 --> 14:23.823
you know, whatever, and...

14:24.625 --> 14:27.530
Could we just... just not...
say anything to him?

14:27.532 --> 14:28.795
Yeah, no, I won't.

14:28.797 --> 14:30.335
-Please, just...?
-Yeah.

14:30.337 --> 14:32.799
Won't say... anything.

14:34.176 --> 14:35.912
Please don't hate me.

14:38.477 --> 14:40.840
I could never hate you.

14:42.481 --> 14:45.251
It's you and me against
the world... always.

14:46.848 --> 14:49.354
Just... no more secrets.

14:50.819 --> 14:52.093
Promise.

14:55.197 --> 14:56.625
Promise.

14:56.627 --> 14:57.901
Okay.

15:00.664 --> 15:02.169
(Dawn): Like this.

15:03.667 --> 15:05.172
That's it!

15:05.174 --> 15:06.338
You're a natural.

15:06.340 --> 15:07.636
(Mia): Uncle Noah!

15:07.638 --> 15:09.044
Auntie Ashley!

15:10.377 --> 15:12.872
Hey, Nugget. I've missed you.

15:13.215 --> 15:14.379
Hi!

15:16.482 --> 15:21.683
(soft music)

15:26.756 --> 15:28.624
You look good, Son.

15:29.693 --> 15:31.561
Oh, really good.

15:37.899 --> 15:39.008
(Jared): Hm.

15:41.243 --> 15:43.738
"Hey, Ashley,
you look good, too."

15:43.740 --> 15:45.905
Hey, Ashley,
you look good, too.

15:45.907 --> 15:47.577
Oh, thanks, Dad.

15:48.283 --> 15:50.613
Okay! Everyone to the table.

15:50.881 --> 15:52.813
Time for<i> kaiseki.</i>

15:55.521 --> 15:57.818
(classical piano music)

15:57.820 --> 15:58.995
Thank you.

16:02.891 --> 16:04.297
(Noah):
Thank you, Dawn.

16:05.069 --> 16:06.431
Wow.

16:13.902 --> 16:15.242
(Dawn): Just in case.

16:15.244 --> 16:16.980
(all chuckle)

16:20.876 --> 16:23.184
This is<i> sakizuke,</i>
the appetizer.

16:23.186 --> 16:25.714
Miso-marinated tofu
with grilled aubergine

16:25.716 --> 16:27.320
and seasonal vegetables.

16:27.322 --> 16:29.454
This is the first dish
I learned to make

16:29.456 --> 16:31.555
when I started
my training in Japan.

16:32.426 --> 16:35.559
Oh, Dawn, this is like
a work of art.

16:35.561 --> 16:37.528
Your guests
must go crazy for this.

16:38.828 --> 16:40.894
She closed her restaurant.

16:41.864 --> 16:43.072
A toast.

16:46.176 --> 16:49.342
We are so happy you all joined
us tonight for a family dinner.

16:49.344 --> 16:50.574
It's so important.

16:51.109 --> 16:52.807
I am so sorry my work kept me

16:52.809 --> 16:54.479
from being home for dinner

16:54.481 --> 16:56.217
so often.

16:56.452 --> 16:58.417
And breakfast. And lunch.

16:58.419 --> 17:00.551
(Jared chuckles)

17:01.353 --> 17:04.654
-Sorry, I was just...
-(Charles): No, no.
You're right.

17:04.656 --> 17:06.095
It's inexcusable.

17:07.857 --> 17:09.197
I loved my job.

17:10.530 --> 17:12.365
But you're my children.

17:13.236 --> 17:15.665
And I should've been
here for you.

17:20.375 --> 17:21.902
(chuckles ruefully)

17:22.773 --> 17:24.707
I should've been here.

17:27.283 --> 17:30.009
Oh, well, that's not
much of a toast, is it?

17:30.011 --> 17:31.879
What I'm trying to say is...

17:32.681 --> 17:38.358
we are so happy
all of you could join us.

17:38.693 --> 17:41.064
It means the world to us.

17:41.825 --> 17:43.198
To family.

17:43.761 --> 17:45.398
(all): To family.

17:45.400 --> 17:46.927
To... family.

17:51.241 --> 17:53.175
(Ashley):
Oh, my God, I'm gonna burst.

17:53.177 --> 17:54.473
Please tell me that's it.

17:54.708 --> 17:56.640
(laughs)
Still one more course,

17:56.642 --> 17:57.971
the<i> mizumono.</i>

17:58.206 --> 17:59.940
A very small dessert.

17:59.942 --> 18:02.514
So before dessert, I, um...

18:03.583 --> 18:06.452
I do have something that, uh,
I want to say to everyone.

18:06.454 --> 18:09.587
And we can't wait to hear it,
but first...

18:09.589 --> 18:11.226
I think these two
need to tell us

18:11.228 --> 18:12.920
what the fuck
we're all doing here.

18:12.922 --> 18:14.086
Rachel.

18:14.088 --> 18:15.197
(Rachel): What?!

18:15.199 --> 18:17.595
You invited us here for this...

18:17.597 --> 18:19.927
fabulous fancy dinner,

18:19.929 --> 18:22.765
told us we couldn't invite
anybody, what is going on?

18:28.344 --> 18:30.245
We've decided to enlist.

18:32.876 --> 18:34.414
What...?

18:34.816 --> 18:36.383
Mia, go watch TV.

18:36.385 --> 18:38.781
-No, I want to stay.
-Mia, go.

18:38.783 --> 18:41.883
That's why we wanted
only adults here this evening.

18:42.085 --> 18:44.017
(Rachel): Well, if you would've
given me a heads-up

18:44.019 --> 18:45.359
on what this night
was all about,

18:45.361 --> 18:46.954
I would've found
a fucking sitter.

18:46.956 --> 18:49.561
-Rachel, watch your mouth.
-Are you fucking kidding me?

18:49.563 --> 18:50.958
You've got a lot of nerve

18:50.960 --> 18:52.234
telling me to watch my fucking--

18:52.236 --> 18:53.961
Watch! Your! Mouth!

18:59.309 --> 19:01.144
Save my dessert.

19:01.938 --> 19:03.311
No social media.

19:04.072 --> 19:05.610
I'm sorry.

19:07.581 --> 19:08.943
I'm sorry.

19:09.545 --> 19:12.815
If you'd like to talk about
this in a respectful manner,

19:13.117 --> 19:14.718
we're here for questions.

19:14.720 --> 19:16.654
Yeah, I'll go first.
Uh, why?

19:16.656 --> 19:19.624
Why would you enlist?

19:19.626 --> 19:20.856
You don't need the money.

19:21.625 --> 19:24.629
(Charles):
For over three decades
I delivered the evening news,

19:24.631 --> 19:26.235
and there was not a week
that went by

19:26.237 --> 19:28.699
where I was not reporting
on some horrific

19:28.701 --> 19:30.437
ecological disaster.

19:30.939 --> 19:33.671
Droughts, floods, wildfires.

19:33.673 --> 19:35.002
Crumbling glaciers.

19:35.604 --> 19:37.675
I remember vividly staring
into my monitor

19:37.677 --> 19:39.281
the day that
the Amazon rainforest

19:39.283 --> 19:41.811
burnt out of existence,
just gone.

19:42.748 --> 19:44.484
And I knew full well

19:44.486 --> 19:46.255
that the last thing
this planet needed

19:46.257 --> 19:47.685
was more people.

19:47.687 --> 19:49.390
And what did I do?
I had children.

19:49.392 --> 19:51.117
-(Charles): Four of them.
-Oh, my God!

19:51.119 --> 19:52.822
(Rachel laughs)

19:52.824 --> 19:54.494
(Charles): And now,
the government is talking about

19:54.496 --> 19:56.155
drafting people
to be euthanized.

19:56.157 --> 19:58.157
If any of your names
were called,

19:58.159 --> 19:59.928
I couldn't live with myself.

19:59.930 --> 20:02.304
-They won't call our names.
-(Charles): You don't know that.

20:02.306 --> 20:03.899
I do, I do, I do.

20:04.201 --> 20:08.211
And even if they did,
they can't call all of us.

20:09.147 --> 20:11.445
Okay, I'm not supposed to say
any of this yet,

20:11.447 --> 20:13.612
but the legislation only permits
one person per family.

20:14.147 --> 20:15.845
That means if one of us
were called,

20:15.847 --> 20:17.385
the rest of us would be safe.

20:17.387 --> 20:19.882
And if at that point
you felt inclined

20:19.884 --> 20:22.984
to take one of our places,
you could,

20:22.986 --> 20:24.821
because they're going
to let parents do that.

20:25.490 --> 20:27.329
But none of that's gonna happen

20:27.331 --> 20:30.189
because these rules aren't made
for people like us.

20:30.691 --> 20:32.598
So let's just fucking forget it.

20:33.667 --> 20:34.996
We can't take that chance.

20:34.998 --> 20:36.635
Oh, my God.

20:36.637 --> 20:39.099
Both our first marriages
ended tragically.

20:39.401 --> 20:41.739
Neither of us ever expected
to find love again,

20:41.741 --> 20:43.708
but by the grace of God, we did.

20:45.415 --> 20:48.207
And we think this is
the right thing to do.

20:48.209 --> 20:51.815
Okay, I'm going to try
my hardest not to swear.

20:51.817 --> 20:56.424
Um, but Dawn, why would you
agree to this bullshit?

21:02.157 --> 21:05.664
Well, we were thinking
we're both public figures,

21:05.666 --> 21:10.537
and we believe if we do this,
we can set a good example.

21:10.539 --> 21:12.231
(Ashley): Oh, my God.

21:12.233 --> 21:14.739
This is about elevating
the York name, isn't it?

21:14.741 --> 21:15.905
(Charles): No, it's not.

21:15.907 --> 21:17.544
It's about doing
the right thing.

21:17.546 --> 21:18.809
No, it's not.

21:19.244 --> 21:22.109
It's about the fact that
we all embarrass you.

21:22.111 --> 21:23.616
(Rachel scoffs)

21:23.618 --> 21:25.783
-What?
-It's true.

21:25.785 --> 21:28.423
I mean, much to your obvious
disappointment,

21:28.425 --> 21:30.920
none of us turned out
to be anything special,

21:30.922 --> 21:34.594
so enlisting is
your way of going out

21:34.596 --> 21:36.222
with the York name
forever remembered

21:36.224 --> 21:39.093
as the epitome
of self-sacrifice.

21:40.470 --> 21:44.197
Dawn, be honest with me:
this wasn't your idea, right?

21:44.738 --> 21:46.375
My dad convinced you?

21:46.377 --> 21:47.541
We decided together.

21:47.543 --> 21:48.905
Bullshit.

21:48.907 --> 21:50.808
Everybody just leave Dawn alone.

21:50.810 --> 21:52.645
I'm sorry, I can't do this.
I just--

21:52.647 --> 21:54.482
-Son! Sit down.
-(Noah): I gotta go.

21:54.484 --> 21:56.275
Please stay. Please!

21:56.277 --> 21:57.485
No, this is not...

21:59.280 --> 22:01.918
Dad... dad, you just said...

22:02.620 --> 22:05.823
You just said that you want
to spend more time with us?

22:05.825 --> 22:09.662
And, and... this doesn't make
any... any fucking sense!

22:09.664 --> 22:10.927
It doesn't make any sense!

22:10.929 --> 22:13.369
Noah, stop! Put that down!

22:14.999 --> 22:17.131
(cane clatters loudly)

22:20.477 --> 22:23.203
We'll continue this discussion
after dessert.

22:23.205 --> 22:25.040
-Right, dessert!
-Yeah.

22:25.675 --> 22:27.977
(Dawn): I will come and get you
when it's ready.

22:31.521 --> 22:33.422
(TV reporter):<i> The rioting</i>
<i> continued throughout the night</i>

22:33.424 --> 22:35.281
<i> with protestors vowing</i>
<i> not to give up</i>

22:35.283 --> 22:37.283
<i> until the government</i>
<i> provides transparency</i>

22:37.285 --> 22:39.087
<i> into the full extent</i>
<i> of D.O.C.S. powers.</i>

22:39.456 --> 22:40.891
<i> We'll be right back.</i>

22:42.160 --> 22:46.292
(male announcer):
<i> Week 39 Enlisters of the Week</i>
<i> are Luis and Rosa Gonzalez.</i>

22:46.294 --> 22:49.702
<i> Luis was employed as a high</i>
<i> school custodian for 25 years,</i>

22:49.704 --> 22:53.200
<i> while Rosa stayed home</i>
<i> and raised their son, Ignacio.</i>

22:53.202 --> 22:56.544
<i> Luis and Rosa bestowed their</i>
<i> enlistment benefit payments</i>

22:56.546 --> 22:59.008
<i> to Ignacio and</i>
<i> his new bride, Maria,</i>

22:59.010 --> 23:01.384
<i> who plan to use the money</i>
<i> to buy their first home.</i>

23:01.652 --> 23:04.849
<i> Luis and Rosa, a grateful</i>
<i> nation thanks you.</i>

23:04.851 --> 23:06.213
(A door closes.)

23:11.660 --> 23:13.627
(Noah): Dad, look,
you don't have to do this.

23:13.629 --> 23:15.024
I have a friend
in the program.

23:15.026 --> 23:16.630
He says the government is lying

23:16.632 --> 23:17.994
about the enlistment numbers.

23:17.996 --> 23:19.358
(Jared): Oh, fuck, here we go.

23:19.360 --> 23:21.063
Conspiracy theory time,
is it?

23:21.065 --> 23:22.196
(Noah):
He's not a wacko, Jared.

23:22.198 --> 23:23.967
He works for a watchdog group,

23:23.969 --> 23:25.397
and Dad, what they're saying
is that way more

23:25.399 --> 23:26.772
than 9% of people
have enlisted.

23:26.774 --> 23:28.477
It's more like 16%.

23:28.479 --> 23:30.545
Yeah, what's this person's name?

23:30.547 --> 23:31.909
His name, why?

23:31.911 --> 23:33.680
(Jared): Because people
who spread disinformation

23:33.682 --> 23:35.880
should be held accountable,
so what's his name?

23:35.882 --> 23:37.376
His name is the same as mine.

23:37.378 --> 23:38.520
He's anonymous.

23:38.522 --> 23:39.950
Oh, he's anonymous.

23:39.952 --> 23:41.688
Those ones
are always the bravest.

23:41.690 --> 23:43.316
I assume you told
this fucking clown

23:43.318 --> 23:45.252
he has no idea
what he's talking about.

23:45.254 --> 23:46.594
(Charles):
How do you know?

23:47.894 --> 23:49.322
You don't know this person.

23:50.094 --> 23:51.698
No, but I do know

23:51.700 --> 23:54.327
this person is speaking
utter nonsense.

23:54.329 --> 23:56.934
Why would the government
lie about that?

23:57.508 --> 23:58.936
Why would they lie?

23:59.438 --> 24:01.169
You do know who's enlisting,
don't you?

24:01.171 --> 24:02.709
And it's only gotten worse

24:02.711 --> 24:04.139
since they opened up enlistment

24:04.141 --> 24:05.481
to undocumented immigrants.

24:05.483 --> 24:08.110
Now, that's a very unfair
picture you're painting.

24:08.112 --> 24:09.980
That's a very popular program.

24:09.982 --> 24:12.620
First off,
those people are paid.

24:12.622 --> 24:13.885
Second off,

24:13.887 --> 24:15.282
their children are fast-tracked

24:15.284 --> 24:16.624
toward citizenship.

24:16.626 --> 24:18.890
-"Those people"?
-(Jared): Oh, for fuck's sakes,

24:18.892 --> 24:20.056
that's not what I meant.

24:20.058 --> 24:22.564
I just meant it is a...

24:22.566 --> 24:25.534
very good opportunity
for people...

24:27.967 --> 24:28.966
like him.

24:29.468 --> 24:31.265
Jared, he is your brother.

24:31.267 --> 24:33.300
(Jared): I said "like him,"
I don't mean him.

24:33.302 --> 24:35.170
He's got all the opportunity
he needs.

24:35.172 --> 24:36.743
Rachel, please help me out here.

24:36.745 --> 24:38.008
No. Never, never.

24:38.010 --> 24:40.747
Okay, guys, I know that,
yeah, times are grim

24:40.749 --> 24:42.441
and rumours are swirling.

24:42.443 --> 24:44.916
But this administration

24:44.918 --> 24:47.952
would never fabricate
enlistment numbers

24:47.954 --> 24:50.185
just to gerrymander,
trust me!

24:51.859 --> 24:53.122
Why should we trust you?

24:54.091 --> 24:56.565
You're on TV every day
defending a government

24:56.567 --> 24:58.600
that is made up
of the same buffoons

24:58.602 --> 25:00.228
who would come onto my show

25:00.230 --> 25:02.505
and deny that climate change
even existed.

25:02.807 --> 25:05.805
I don't know why I expected
anything different from you.

25:05.807 --> 25:08.137
You spent an entire career
in mainstream media

25:08.139 --> 25:09.402
just pointing fingers.

25:11.846 --> 25:15.045
Asking questions
is not pointing fingers.

25:15.614 --> 25:17.784
Pointing fingers is when
this administration

25:17.786 --> 25:23.086
repeatedly refers to this crisis
as the "Asian Collapse."

25:23.088 --> 25:25.352
But that's true!

25:25.354 --> 25:27.860
China, Japan, India,
they're responsible for this!

25:27.862 --> 25:29.158
Shame on you!

25:30.425 --> 25:32.029
That sort of hateful rhetoric

25:32.031 --> 25:33.833
is why Dawn can't even
go outside anymore.

25:33.835 --> 25:35.494
For God's sake!

25:36.029 --> 25:38.035
They burned down her restaurant.

25:41.579 --> 25:44.712
Oh, I know you crave
the spotlight, Jared.

25:48.542 --> 25:50.553
But you're
embarrassing yourself.

25:51.512 --> 25:53.215
And you embarrass me.

25:53.217 --> 25:54.480
Okay, cool.

25:54.482 --> 25:55.481
So, I guess next time

25:55.483 --> 25:56.691
I go on television,

25:56.693 --> 25:57.956
I should just make a pit stop

25:57.958 --> 25:59.353
at one of Noah's meetings

25:59.355 --> 26:01.795
and just see what the deadbeat
junkies have to say?

26:01.797 --> 26:02.994
Jared, shut up!

26:02.996 --> 26:04.457
He met his girlfriend
at a meeting.

26:07.033 --> 26:09.165
(laughs)

26:10.003 --> 26:11.706
You're dating another addict?

26:13.402 --> 26:14.610
Son?

26:19.881 --> 26:22.244
(exhales sharply)
Her name is Grace.

26:23.214 --> 26:24.884
And um...

26:25.553 --> 26:29.086
she... she's been clean
for 10 years, Dad.

26:29.088 --> 26:30.549
And...

26:30.951 --> 26:33.057
she's been very,
very good for me.

26:37.030 --> 26:38.392
Do you have a picture?

26:39.395 --> 26:40.735
(sighs)

26:41.562 --> 26:42.561
Yeah.

26:47.909 --> 26:49.436
(Charles):
Well, she's lovely.

26:49.771 --> 26:50.976
What does she do?

26:51.912 --> 26:54.947
She's a manager at Sports World
at the Oakwood Mall.

26:56.511 --> 26:57.950
And...

26:59.415 --> 27:01.118
I work there, too.

27:01.120 --> 27:04.385
Um... I play the piano
in the food court.

27:04.387 --> 27:05.925
You're playing again?

27:05.927 --> 27:08.389
(Jared):
Just jazz standards and Muzak.

27:08.391 --> 27:09.797
You know, it's nothing.

27:09.799 --> 27:11.491
No, it's not nothing.

27:12.967 --> 27:14.197
It's perfect.

27:16.674 --> 27:18.135
Well, I better go help Dawn.

27:21.173 --> 27:23.107
(Jared):
Anyone else see the way he...

27:23.109 --> 27:25.373
bandied about
that fireplace poker?

27:25.375 --> 27:26.979
I thought he was gonna kill me.

27:26.981 --> 27:28.310
Can I see?

27:29.412 --> 27:31.687
(eerie music)

27:47.166 --> 27:49.804
(Ashley):
Oh! My God!

27:49.806 --> 27:53.368
(indistinct chatter)

27:54.910 --> 27:56.272
She's gone.

28:00.850 --> 28:02.311
(Rachel): What?

28:04.920 --> 28:08.724
"I'm sorry, I can't do it.
I will always love you, Dawn."

28:09.026 --> 28:11.122
What does she mean,
"I can't do it"?

28:13.027 --> 28:15.060
Dad, did you already sign up?

28:15.733 --> 28:17.623
(doorbell)

28:22.872 --> 28:24.432
Hi, I'm Bob.

28:25.336 --> 28:27.072
(Mia): It's them!

28:27.074 --> 28:28.744
-Oh, they're early.
-(Ashley): What?

28:30.847 --> 28:33.375
(tense music)

28:36.380 --> 28:37.643
(knocking on door)

28:37.645 --> 28:39.249
(Bob):
Hey, Bob from D.O.C.S.,

28:39.251 --> 28:41.152
Department of Citizen Strategy.

28:41.154 --> 28:42.648
I'm sorry we're a bit early.

28:42.650 --> 28:44.353
Our last appointment
was a no-show.

28:44.355 --> 28:45.992
You scheduled it for tonight?

28:46.494 --> 28:47.961
We wanted you all here with us

28:47.963 --> 28:49.688
as we said goodbye.

28:49.690 --> 28:51.558
What the fuck, Dad!

28:51.560 --> 28:53.659
-You can't just spring
that on us!
-(knock at door)

28:53.661 --> 28:56.563
Tell him to leave!
We're not done here.

28:56.565 --> 28:58.730
(heavy knocking)

28:58.732 --> 28:59.907
Jesus!

29:01.009 --> 29:02.371
Hi. Bob again.

29:02.373 --> 29:04.175
We can't park our vehicle
in the driveway

29:04.177 --> 29:05.374
with all the cars.

29:05.376 --> 29:06.243
Mind if we park it

29:06.245 --> 29:07.739
along the side here?

29:07.741 --> 29:09.411
It's a tight fit,
but Tony's a pro.

29:09.820 --> 29:11.380
Uh... sure.

29:11.382 --> 29:13.613
-Yeah, okay, Tony, we're good.
-Alright.

29:14.182 --> 29:17.485
Well... normally, I'd start
by asking who people are,

29:17.487 --> 29:19.421
but I... I certainly know
who you are, sir.

29:19.423 --> 29:21.159
I'm a big fan.

29:21.161 --> 29:22.897
"Charles York: Most Reliable
Source for News."

29:22.899 --> 29:25.559
Is that James Earl Jones
who does that voice?

29:25.561 --> 29:27.561
No, that's CNN.
That was years ago.

29:27.563 --> 29:29.167
Anyway, I love it.
I love it.

29:29.169 --> 29:31.763
It makes you want
to listen, you know?

29:31.765 --> 29:33.666
Uh...
(whistles)

29:33.668 --> 29:35.437
Wow!
You're married to Dawn Kim.

29:35.439 --> 29:37.241
I saw her on Iron Chef.

29:37.243 --> 29:38.704
Me and the missus
have always wanted

29:38.706 --> 29:40.244
to go to her restaurant,

29:40.246 --> 29:42.048
but just a little too rich
for our blood, you know.

29:42.050 --> 29:43.544
Anyway.
Do you mind if I come in,

29:43.546 --> 29:45.150
or did you want to do
the procedures

29:45.152 --> 29:46.921
in the driveway?
(laughs)

29:47.256 --> 29:48.351
(clears throat)

29:48.886 --> 29:50.254
I'm so sorry. That was rude.

29:50.256 --> 29:51.387
That was rude.

29:51.756 --> 29:53.620
I'm just a little
out of sorts these days.

29:53.622 --> 29:56.128
It's just impossible to take
time off right now.

29:56.530 --> 29:59.758
(whistles)
Circling back. May I come in?

30:00.970 --> 30:02.431
Please. Come in.

30:02.766 --> 30:04.136
Hello. I'm Bob.

30:04.138 --> 30:05.533
-Hi.
-Hello.

30:05.535 --> 30:07.106
Hello.

30:08.472 --> 30:10.175
(whistles)
Wow!

30:10.771 --> 30:12.276
This place is stunning.

30:12.811 --> 30:14.641
I don't get to see inside
a lot of houses

30:14.643 --> 30:15.774
in this neighbourhood.

30:16.409 --> 30:18.249
I love how you've updated things

30:18.251 --> 30:19.987
and kept the historical
elements.

30:20.489 --> 30:22.649
And that chandelier just, like--
(sniffs)

30:22.651 --> 30:23.925
Fish?

30:23.927 --> 30:26.686
Yes. Uh, hi, I'm Jared.

30:26.688 --> 30:28.490
I'm Charles's son.

30:28.492 --> 30:29.865
I know you.
You're on TV, too.

30:29.867 --> 30:32.263
I... I am!
Yeah, lately, anyway.

30:32.265 --> 30:33.935
You're that government guy.

30:33.937 --> 30:36.234
Well, no. I'm...
I'm an anthropologist.

30:36.236 --> 30:37.565
But I have been working
in coordination

30:37.567 --> 30:38.797
with the government.

30:38.799 --> 30:40.205
Ah, that's great.
Where's Dawn?

30:40.207 --> 30:41.943
Uh, she's not here.

30:41.945 --> 30:44.077
She got cold feet and she left.

30:44.079 --> 30:45.980
Oh. So it's just you, then.

30:45.982 --> 30:49.412
Yes. But my wife and I decided
to enlist together,

30:49.414 --> 30:51.282
so if it's alright with you,

30:51.284 --> 30:53.317
I'd like to ask you
to come back another time.

30:53.319 --> 30:54.813
I'm sure once she and I connect,

30:54.815 --> 30:56.320
she'll be back on board.

31:04.594 --> 31:07.034
That's... that's great.
Yeah, right.

31:07.369 --> 31:10.235
Do you... uh, can I talk to you
in private for a sec?

31:11.568 --> 31:13.040
I mean, don't worry.
Don't worry.

31:13.042 --> 31:14.833
Just need to sign some
confidential paperwork

31:14.835 --> 31:15.867
to cancel the procedure.

31:15.869 --> 31:17.176
You know the government

31:17.178 --> 31:18.441
and their paperwork?

31:18.443 --> 31:20.113
Like a dog with a bone.
(barks)

31:20.115 --> 31:22.610
Absolutely.
I'll sign whatever.

31:23.349 --> 31:24.579
Please follow me.

31:26.847 --> 31:28.781
(Bob): Just initial the bottom
of each page,

31:28.783 --> 31:30.959
sign the last one,
and we're all set.

31:32.820 --> 31:34.897
Fine. Well...

31:35.999 --> 31:37.790
I'd like to look it over first.

31:37.792 --> 31:39.627
Sure. Take your time.

31:40.696 --> 31:42.597
(Bob whistles)

31:44.073 --> 31:46.304
Wow. That's Mandela.

31:46.306 --> 31:47.569
I recognize him.

31:48.341 --> 31:49.703
And Bono.

31:51.146 --> 31:53.982
Whew! Is that Queen B?

31:53.984 --> 31:55.918
Oh, my God, I love her.
It is, isn't it?

31:56.253 --> 31:59.284
Oh, what a life
you've led, my friend.

31:59.286 --> 32:00.879
By all accounts,
a virtuous one.

32:00.881 --> 32:02.023
Not everyone can say that.

32:02.025 --> 32:03.552
Some men in your position,

32:03.554 --> 32:05.389
well, they take advantage.

32:05.391 --> 32:09.228
Lives ruined, careers destroyed,
and all for what?

32:09.230 --> 32:11.659
A little...
a little hanky-panky.

32:11.661 --> 32:12.968
Yeah.

32:13.470 --> 32:15.366
When those bozos are gone,

32:15.368 --> 32:17.764
all anyone is gonna remember
is the nasty stuff.

32:20.043 --> 32:21.306
Not you.

32:21.574 --> 32:22.802
When you're gone,

32:22.804 --> 32:24.276
people are gonna remember you

32:24.278 --> 32:25.508
as one of the greats.

32:25.776 --> 32:27.642
That is unless something
comes to light

32:27.644 --> 32:29.545
that makes people
see you differently.

32:31.351 --> 32:32.779
What is this?

32:33.281 --> 32:34.814
I'm not signing this.

32:35.421 --> 32:37.454
Do you know who I am?

32:37.753 --> 32:39.258
I do.

32:39.260 --> 32:40.919
As I said, I'm a big fan,

32:40.921 --> 32:43.460
and I will never stop feeling
that way toward you.

32:44.095 --> 32:46.298
No matter what list
your name is on.

32:47.400 --> 32:50.731
(sinister music)

32:50.733 --> 32:53.800
(inaudible chatter)

33:02.316 --> 33:05.119
(♪♪)

33:16.957 --> 33:21.003
(mournful music)

33:28.606 --> 33:30.903
The way he plays...

33:31.741 --> 33:33.114
it's beautiful.

33:33.116 --> 33:34.874
Dad, I don't understand.

33:35.309 --> 33:37.811
You said that you wanted
to do this with Dawn.

33:38.451 --> 33:39.978
What changed?

33:40.447 --> 33:42.552
-Did he...?
-Oh, no. No, no, no, no.

33:42.554 --> 33:43.718
And you were right.

33:44.487 --> 33:46.391
I did try to convince
Dawn to enlist.

33:47.060 --> 33:49.526
But I'm still set on doing this.

33:54.071 --> 33:56.302
I'm sorry I wasn't
a better father.

33:56.964 --> 33:59.668
I was too hard on all of you.

34:00.473 --> 34:03.309
Especially
after your mother died.

34:09.713 --> 34:13.649
The estate will be divided
evenly amongst you all.

34:17.985 --> 34:20.557
-Be good to one another.
-(Mia crying): Mom!

34:20.992 --> 34:22.790
(Charles):
Support one another.

34:25.861 --> 34:27.432
Do better than I did.

34:28.402 --> 34:31.766
(Noah continues to play
the piano)

34:48.422 --> 34:50.092
(Bob):
This is the anaesthetic.

34:51.755 --> 34:53.491
Once I administer it,

34:53.493 --> 34:56.197
you'll fall asleep
and you won't feel a thing.

35:24.458 --> 35:26.590
(piano playing ends)

35:30.662 --> 35:33.201
(Mia): Grandpa!
(crying)

35:35.535 --> 35:36.897
(loud clatter)

35:38.934 --> 35:40.934
(gurney wheels squeak)

35:48.944 --> 35:50.482
(door slams)

35:50.484 --> 35:52.110
(Bob):
That was very moving.

35:52.112 --> 35:53.947
From the music
to the reconciliations.

35:53.949 --> 35:56.290
I mean, that procedure
ranked right up there

35:56.292 --> 35:57.654
with the best of them.

35:58.085 --> 35:59.359
Just go.

36:00.824 --> 36:02.164
Alright, then.

36:02.793 --> 36:03.957
Bye.

36:05.664 --> 36:08.302
Oh... I can't leave quite yet.

36:08.304 --> 36:09.501
Why not?

36:09.503 --> 36:11.305
You're not gonna like this.

36:11.307 --> 36:13.131
But I need a second cadaver.

36:15.872 --> 36:17.839
A body. I need a second body.

36:17.841 --> 36:19.544
No, I already told you:
Dawn left.

36:19.546 --> 36:21.414
No, and that's unfortunate.

36:21.416 --> 36:23.647
But we're here to collect, um...

36:23.649 --> 36:25.682
two bodies.

36:25.684 --> 36:27.046
What's he talking about?

36:27.648 --> 36:29.950
You're scaring my niece.
Get out.

36:29.952 --> 36:31.622
Fine, fine...

36:32.152 --> 36:34.152
(tense music)

36:35.496 --> 36:37.089
-Holy shit!
-(Ashley): Oh, my God!

36:37.091 --> 36:39.058
-(Rachel): Jesus Christ!
-(Bob): Calm down, calm down.

36:39.060 --> 36:41.335
-Mom!
-(Bob): It's alright.

36:41.337 --> 36:43.502
Look, we've got three hours
until our next appointment,

36:43.504 --> 36:46.131
then it's... what?
Roughly a half hour from here.

36:46.133 --> 36:48.342
Another half hour to perform
the procedure.

36:48.344 --> 36:50.509
And that leaves you
two full hours to decide

36:50.511 --> 36:52.742
which one of you
is gonna take Dawn's place.

36:54.944 --> 36:56.647
(Jared):
Okay. I don't know if this is

36:56.649 --> 36:58.286
some kind of ill-timed joke,

36:58.288 --> 37:00.519
but it ends now.

37:00.521 --> 37:04.050
Uh... I'm calling some friends
of mine in the Administration.

37:04.052 --> 37:06.294
Yeah, that's not gonna happen.
We scrambled the house.

37:07.121 --> 37:08.494
We can't have you wasting time

37:08.496 --> 37:09.957
when you should be concentrating

37:09.959 --> 37:11.156
on the task at hand.

37:11.158 --> 37:12.894
Now the little one here.
Mia, right?

37:12.896 --> 37:14.500
You don't talk to her.

37:14.502 --> 37:16.799
Relax. I was just gonna
tell you that she's exempt.

37:16.801 --> 37:19.131
We don't get paid for minors.

37:19.738 --> 37:21.199
Paid?

37:21.201 --> 37:22.673
Well, sure.

37:22.675 --> 37:24.411
D.O.C.S. contracts out
cadaver collections

37:24.413 --> 37:25.973
to private companies

37:25.975 --> 37:28.316
such as the one that employs me
and my colleagues here.

37:28.318 --> 37:30.175
We used to work in Corrections,

37:30.177 --> 37:31.649
but prisons emptied out
in a hurry

37:31.651 --> 37:32.914
when enlistment opened up

37:32.916 --> 37:34.487
to incarcerated convicts.

37:34.489 --> 37:35.686
It's such a shame, too.

37:35.688 --> 37:37.853
Housing, feeding convicts
over time

37:37.855 --> 37:40.394
paid a lot more dough
than cadaver procurement.

37:40.396 --> 37:42.495
That's strictly a one-time fee,

37:42.497 --> 37:44.497
and currently, the government
isn't paying for minors.

37:44.499 --> 37:46.961
But maybe some day soon,
right, Professor?

37:47.766 --> 37:49.194
You're a lunatic.

37:49.471 --> 37:50.767
No!

37:51.169 --> 37:53.869
I'm doing my job, just like you.

37:55.609 --> 37:57.444
-Now give us the girl.
-Mom?

37:57.446 --> 37:58.709
It's okay.

37:58.711 --> 38:00.007
You're not taking her.

38:00.009 --> 38:01.448
-(Noah grunts)
-Uncle Noah!

38:01.450 --> 38:02.317
(Bob):
Tony, take her.

38:02.319 --> 38:03.384
-Mom?
-No!

38:03.386 --> 38:04.682
You're not taking her!

38:04.684 --> 38:07.047
-You can't have her!
-It's okay, it's alright.

38:07.049 --> 38:08.213
We're not gonna hurt her.

38:08.215 --> 38:09.753
You have my word.

38:09.755 --> 38:11.425
She's gonna sit with us
in our vehicle

38:11.427 --> 38:12.789
until this situation
is resolved.

38:12.791 --> 38:14.560
Now trust me.

38:14.562 --> 38:16.496
You don't want her here
for this next part.

38:18.093 --> 38:21.127
Okay, Mia, listen to me.

38:21.129 --> 38:22.733
You need to go
with the man, okay?

38:22.735 --> 38:24.064
No, no, Mom, I'm so scared.

38:24.066 --> 38:25.230
It's okay.

38:25.232 --> 38:26.572
We just need to figure this out.

38:26.574 --> 38:27.639
I promise.

38:27.641 --> 38:28.871
Okay? Come on.

38:29.940 --> 38:31.544
(Bob): Let's go.

38:31.546 --> 38:33.073
(Ashley):
You're gonna be okay.

38:34.417 --> 38:36.043
Why are you doing this?

38:36.045 --> 38:37.308
We didn't enlist. Dawn did.

38:37.310 --> 38:38.980
Please go find her.

38:38.982 --> 38:40.784
We already have people
looking for Dawn,

38:40.786 --> 38:43.017
but the odds that she's located
in the next two hours

38:43.019 --> 38:44.656
are not good,

38:44.658 --> 38:46.427
and we are not falling further
below our quota,

38:46.429 --> 38:47.890
no way, no how.

38:47.892 --> 38:49.287
What did you say to our father?

38:49.289 --> 38:50.497
Nothing.

38:50.499 --> 38:51.597
I just gave him the paperwork

38:51.599 --> 38:52.796
to cancel this procedure.

38:52.798 --> 38:53.962
Then he read it over

38:53.964 --> 38:55.062
and decided not to sign.

38:55.064 --> 38:56.668
Which, you know...

38:56.670 --> 38:58.472
See? You can back out
no problem.

38:58.474 --> 38:59.803
But your bank accounts
are frozen,

38:59.805 --> 39:01.332
you lose your assets
and you go to jail

39:01.334 --> 39:03.037
for the rest of your lives.

39:03.039 --> 39:04.445
Either way, my company
gets paid.

39:04.447 --> 39:05.644
Jared, is that true?

39:05.646 --> 39:07.140
Yeah, it is.

39:07.142 --> 39:09.582
Nothing seemed to bother him
as much as the fact

39:09.584 --> 39:11.309
that his name would one day
be published

39:11.311 --> 39:12.750
on the government's
Cowards' List.

39:13.285 --> 39:15.852
Yep, we're gonna let people
know the names of all the bums

39:15.854 --> 39:18.723
who turn their backs on their
country when it mattered most.

39:19.292 --> 39:21.957
Your dad cared a lot about
what people thought of him, huh?

39:25.094 --> 39:26.434
Alright.
(clears throat)

39:26.436 --> 39:27.501
Uh, Bob...

39:27.866 --> 39:29.129
Bob?

39:29.598 --> 39:32.869
Um... you don't have to do this.

39:32.871 --> 39:34.266
-Well...
-(Jared): Okay?

39:34.268 --> 39:38.611
I... I am sure,
as leader of this unit,

39:38.613 --> 39:42.175
you have some discretion as
to how the D.O.C.S. regulations

39:42.177 --> 39:43.341
are applied.

39:44.243 --> 39:47.455
So... I... I'm gonna
tell you this as a favour,

39:48.084 --> 39:49.952
you don't want to do this.

39:49.954 --> 39:51.657
You're on the wrong
side of history.

39:51.659 --> 39:54.693
This... this is a mistake.

39:55.128 --> 39:57.696
(whispering): I know people,
important people.

39:57.698 --> 39:59.731
You know what? You make
a very good point, Jared.

39:59.733 --> 40:01.469
I really appreciate that.
Thank you.

40:01.471 --> 40:02.866
Of course, of course,
no problem.

40:02.868 --> 40:04.065
I hate to be that guy--

40:04.067 --> 40:05.539
Yeah, yeah, but
here's the thing.

40:05.541 --> 40:06.870
I don't care who you know.

40:06.872 --> 40:08.399
And I certainly don't care

40:08.401 --> 40:09.840
for you telling me
how to do my job.

40:09.842 --> 40:11.204
The rules are the same
for everybody.

40:11.206 --> 40:12.645
That's how I roll.

40:13.549 --> 40:15.208
So here's what I suggest.

40:15.210 --> 40:17.111
You all go into separate rooms,

40:17.113 --> 40:19.751
take some time,
think about your lives.

40:20.186 --> 40:23.117
I'm sure one of you
is gonna realize that

40:23.619 --> 40:25.053
it's not all that great.

40:26.023 --> 40:27.858
And to get things started,

40:27.860 --> 40:30.124
I brought a little
reading material.

40:30.126 --> 40:31.532
You see, this situation happens

40:31.534 --> 40:33.501
a lot more often than you think,

40:33.503 --> 40:35.129
and that's why our Familial
Research Department

40:35.131 --> 40:37.802
compiles concise personalized
notes on all family members

40:37.804 --> 40:41.267
based on information gathered
from browser histories,

40:41.269 --> 40:44.039
e-mails, texts,
DMs and phone calls.

40:44.041 --> 40:45.579
And not just from them,

40:45.581 --> 40:47.240
but from the people
they interact with.

40:47.742 --> 40:49.374
So, let's start with Jared York.

40:49.376 --> 40:51.618
-Please don't.
-This is good, this is good.

40:51.620 --> 40:53.378
Your very young girlfriend
Kaylee,

40:53.380 --> 40:55.413
who you abandoned your wife
and child for last year,

40:55.415 --> 40:57.052
she's having carnal relations

40:57.054 --> 40:58.724
with three to five
additional people,

40:58.726 --> 40:59.857
depending on the week.

40:59.859 --> 41:01.089
She's what?

41:01.091 --> 41:02.255
Speaking of your son, Lucas,

41:02.257 --> 41:03.861
he hopes that you'll enlist

41:03.863 --> 41:05.126
so he never has to see your,

41:05.128 --> 41:06.259
and I quote here,

41:06.261 --> 41:08.569
"stupid AF face again."

41:08.571 --> 41:11.638
-(Jared exhales sharply)
-Oh, and you often Google--

41:11.640 --> 41:12.738
Oh, okay.

41:12.740 --> 41:14.069
You Google shit,
you Google shit.

41:14.071 --> 41:16.775
Next up, Rachel York.

41:16.777 --> 41:19.206
It's okay. I'm pretty sure
I know what's on there.

41:19.208 --> 41:22.583
Um, my daughter is being bullied
because of me.

41:23.476 --> 41:25.146
Yes. Says so right here.

41:25.148 --> 41:27.346
Uh, my board wants to fire me
from my own company.

41:27.348 --> 41:28.754
Yeah, that's--

41:28.756 --> 41:30.019
Oh, and I'm also wanted

41:30.021 --> 41:31.658
for a string of bank robberies?

41:35.158 --> 41:37.092
That's not-- agh!

41:37.094 --> 41:39.424
Fuck you, you piece of shit!

41:39.426 --> 41:41.459
(moans in pain)

41:41.928 --> 41:45.804
Stand down, stand down.
Here, read them yourselves.

41:46.406 --> 41:48.499
Just flick the porch lights
off and on

41:48.501 --> 41:50.138
when you've made your decision.

41:50.140 --> 41:52.646
Wait, wait, uh, what...
what if we can't decide?

41:53.979 --> 41:56.375
What if we can't
make a decision?

41:57.345 --> 41:59.015
I will decide for you.

42:03.824 --> 42:05.252
(Ashley sighs)

42:05.254 --> 42:08.519
(crickets chirping)

42:08.521 --> 42:10.356
(indistinct chatter on radio)

42:15.297 --> 42:17.869
(eerie music)

42:25.406 --> 42:26.878
Shit.

42:58.879 --> 43:02.045
(crickets chirping)

43:05.919 --> 43:07.919
(male voice on radio):
<i> Procedure 16 complete.</i>

43:07.921 --> 43:10.251
<i> Heading to 17's location.</i>
<i> Over.</i>

43:12.728 --> 43:15.256
You know, I'd... I'd ask you
to play cards with me,

43:15.258 --> 43:16.994
but I don't
much appreciate your mom

43:16.996 --> 43:18.699
punching me in the face.

43:18.701 --> 43:20.558
I appreciated it.

43:23.101 --> 43:25.431
(sombre music)

44:13.855 --> 44:15.217
(screaming)

44:15.552 --> 44:19.254
Fuck you! Fuck!

44:19.256 --> 44:20.387
Fuck!

44:20.789 --> 44:23.665
Fuck you, you piece of shit!

44:24.567 --> 44:29.132
What the fuck do you know?!
"Melodramatic," my fucking ass!

44:29.497 --> 44:31.772
Fuck! Agh!

44:32.341 --> 44:34.500
(Ashley yelling indistinctly)

44:37.813 --> 44:39.978
(♪♪)

44:51.585 --> 44:53.651
Yeah... let me...

44:53.653 --> 44:56.489
Come on, Jared.
Come on, Jared.

44:57.360 --> 44:58.799
Come on, Jared.

45:09.141 --> 45:11.812
(Jared): Would you please move?
Thank you.

45:13.607 --> 45:15.244
So, anyone--

45:15.246 --> 45:17.884
Yeah, I think Noah should
sacrifice himself for us.

45:17.886 --> 45:19.083
Screw you, Jared.

45:19.085 --> 45:20.645
No, really? Screw him.

45:20.647 --> 45:21.855
Screw him.

45:21.857 --> 45:23.791
When Mom and Dad adopted him,

45:23.793 --> 45:26.552
he was given every opportunity
under the sun.

45:26.554 --> 45:29.027
He went to the best schools.

45:29.029 --> 45:31.689
He had the top piano
instructors.

45:31.691 --> 45:34.032
But, but...

45:34.034 --> 45:37.695
not only did he piss
his own life away,

45:37.697 --> 45:40.907
he also fucking killed
that woman in the accident!

45:41.470 --> 45:43.371
So, if you ask me,

45:43.373 --> 45:46.176
Noah should
sacrifice himself for us.

45:46.178 --> 45:47.672
It only makes sense.

45:47.674 --> 45:49.575
(Ashley):
No. You know what makes sense?

45:49.577 --> 45:52.248
-Putting it to a vote!
-Okay.

45:52.250 --> 45:55.416
Who here thinks that Jared
should take Dawn's spot?

45:55.418 --> 45:58.056
Jared? How fucking dare you?

45:58.058 --> 45:59.354
I have a child!

45:59.356 --> 46:00.355
(Ashley): Who hates you!

46:00.357 --> 46:01.928
Like everyone else in your life.

46:01.930 --> 46:03.864
Oh, do you know everyone
else in my life?

46:03.866 --> 46:05.459
(Ashley):
Oh, my God, no, maybe I don't.

46:05.461 --> 46:06.933
-But I know Beth.
-(Jared): Hey.

46:06.935 --> 46:08.198
(Ashley):
Oh, you remember her?

46:08.200 --> 46:10.035
Your beautiful,
amazing wife?

46:10.037 --> 46:12.169
The one you bailed on
the second someone showed you

46:12.171 --> 46:13.302
just a little bit of attention?

46:13.304 --> 46:14.105
(Jared): Stop it!

46:14.107 --> 46:15.601
I bet if she were here,

46:15.603 --> 46:17.240
her hand would be held
fucking high!

46:17.242 --> 46:18.373
No, it wouldn't!

46:18.375 --> 46:19.770
Yes, you would!

46:19.772 --> 46:21.673
Stop fighting!

46:29.551 --> 46:31.793
I didn't get to say this
earlier...

46:34.864 --> 46:37.425
but I came here tonight
to apologize.

46:38.194 --> 46:40.263
I've been nothing but a drain
on this family

46:40.265 --> 46:41.429
for far too long.

46:42.399 --> 46:44.432
But the accident woke me up.

46:45.039 --> 46:46.401
I'm clean.

46:47.206 --> 46:48.942
I found love.

46:48.944 --> 46:51.076
And for the first time
in my life,

46:52.409 --> 46:55.212
I see a future for myself.

46:55.852 --> 46:57.445
And I want nothing more

46:57.447 --> 46:59.579
than for that future to include
the people in this room.

46:59.581 --> 47:01.482
We can get through this,
but we have to stick together,

47:01.484 --> 47:02.780
like Dad said.

47:03.893 --> 47:06.487
(scoffs)
Like Dad said?

47:06.489 --> 47:08.027
(Noah):
Before he died.

47:08.029 --> 47:09.897
Dad said to be kind
to one another,

47:09.899 --> 47:11.063
to support one another.

47:11.065 --> 47:12.691
So let's stop fighting,

47:12.693 --> 47:14.231
and let's work together.

47:14.233 --> 47:15.463
It's what Dad would've wanted.

47:15.465 --> 47:17.630
(scoffs)
(Rachel): Are you serious?

47:17.632 --> 47:22.107
That asshole signed one of his
own fucking children up to die.

47:22.109 --> 47:24.208
He couldn't have known
about that, obviously.

47:24.210 --> 47:26.210
Oh, no. Not obviously.

47:26.212 --> 47:29.081
No. Nothing with him
was ever obvious.

47:29.083 --> 47:31.578
The man could've given
a fucking Ted Talk

47:31.580 --> 47:33.349
on withholding,

47:33.351 --> 47:35.450
and all of a sudden,
I'm supposed to give a shit

47:35.452 --> 47:37.716
because he got all weepy
on his deathbed?

47:37.718 --> 47:39.157
Fuck you.

47:42.525 --> 47:44.690
(Jared): Nice, nice.

47:45.528 --> 47:47.198
Now what the fuck do we do?

47:48.201 --> 47:49.794
Where is it? Where is it?

47:50.563 --> 47:52.830
I mean, where is it?
It's gotta be here somewhere.

47:52.832 --> 47:54.667
No, no, no. Is it here?

47:56.110 --> 47:57.978
No, no, no...

47:57.980 --> 47:59.177
There it is!

47:59.179 --> 48:00.772
There's the card I needed.

48:00.774 --> 48:02.213
Why don't you shove it
up your butt

48:02.215 --> 48:03.478
so you'll always have it?

48:03.480 --> 48:05.546
You have your mother's charm.

48:06.714 --> 48:09.319
(radio chatter)

48:09.321 --> 48:11.750
(crickets chirping)

48:15.998 --> 48:18.625
Boss, they blinked the light.

48:18.627 --> 48:20.935
Decision time. BRB.

48:21.170 --> 48:23.630
(tense music)

48:24.468 --> 48:26.600
(door opens, shuts)

48:33.081 --> 48:34.575
Hello! Hi.

48:35.479 --> 48:36.808
We ready to proceed?

48:36.810 --> 48:38.986
No, uh, we just...
we had a question.

48:40.583 --> 48:43.518
You said that if we couldn't
decide who has the procedure,

48:43.520 --> 48:46.026
you'd decide for us.

48:46.395 --> 48:48.424
How will you decide?

48:49.922 --> 48:51.262
Very good question.

48:51.697 --> 48:54.760
You'll be happy to know that
I use a very scientific system

48:54.762 --> 48:56.300
perfected over time.

48:58.271 --> 49:00.073
(Ashley gasps)

49:04.508 --> 49:06.013
(Jared flaps his lips)

49:06.015 --> 49:08.114
What if we gave you a body?

49:10.547 --> 49:12.415
What, did you find one
in the freezer?

49:12.417 --> 49:13.955
No, you fuck.

49:14.490 --> 49:17.783
I'm asking if you have
to do the procedure,

49:17.785 --> 49:20.588
or can we just
deliver you a body?

49:22.955 --> 49:26.429
A procedure is preferable
from a paperwork standpoint.

49:27.064 --> 49:29.927
But I would figure
something out.

49:29.929 --> 49:32.369
(♪♪)

49:32.371 --> 49:35.009
(door opens, shuts)

49:39.411 --> 49:42.511
No, no decision yet.

49:42.942 --> 49:44.645
My cards.

49:44.947 --> 49:46.482
What did you...?

49:46.484 --> 49:49.419
What did you do?
Why would you do this?

49:49.421 --> 49:50.915
Because you're a bully.

49:56.296 --> 49:57.427
What was that about?

49:57.429 --> 49:58.989
What?

49:58.991 --> 50:00.826
You said that we were
just gonna ask Bob

50:00.828 --> 50:01.827
how he would decide?

50:01.829 --> 50:03.235
Yeah. And we did that.

50:03.237 --> 50:05.765
And then, I had a follow-up
question.

50:05.767 --> 50:08.042
(laughs)
A very pointed one.

50:08.044 --> 50:10.341
(Rachel):
No, a very logical one.

50:10.910 --> 50:12.772
I don't want to draw straws,
do you?

50:12.774 --> 50:15.049
Fuckin' no, of course not.
But...

50:16.547 --> 50:18.580
maybe it's what's fair?

50:18.582 --> 50:20.186
Fuck fair.

50:20.688 --> 50:22.980
I don't want a one in four
chance of dying tonight.

50:22.982 --> 50:25.356
Sorry, those odds
don't work for me.

50:25.358 --> 50:28.887
Okay, so what is
your suggestion, then?

50:29.758 --> 50:31.857
I don't have one.

50:32.326 --> 50:36.631
I've made mistakes,
a lot of them,

50:36.633 --> 50:38.996
especially recently.

50:38.998 --> 50:42.472
But I am sure as hell not ready
to throw in the towel.

50:43.002 --> 50:45.112
None of us are!

50:45.114 --> 50:48.379
That's kind of beside
the point, isn't it?

50:48.381 --> 50:50.007
(Rachel): No, it isn't.

50:50.647 --> 50:52.350
Because here's the thing.

50:52.852 --> 50:55.980
I barely know
you fucking people.

50:57.819 --> 51:00.127
I know we're family
and all, but what?

51:00.129 --> 51:04.461
We see each other three,
maybe four times a year?

51:04.463 --> 51:06.298
Always here at Dad's.

51:06.300 --> 51:08.729
I mean, we never get
together on our own.

51:08.731 --> 51:10.335
We never even call each other

51:10.337 --> 51:12.601
unless it's an obligatory
birthday call.

51:12.603 --> 51:15.835
I am closer with the lady
who does my nails

51:15.837 --> 51:18.002
than I am with any of you.

51:18.004 --> 51:19.740
What's your point?

51:21.249 --> 51:23.447
My point is...

51:23.449 --> 51:26.043
if Bob needs a second body,

51:26.045 --> 51:28.221
I can tell you all
right fucking now,

51:28.223 --> 51:29.651
it's not gonna be mine.

51:29.653 --> 51:32.588
-(Jared): Holy fuck!
-(indistinct yelling)

51:33.789 --> 51:34.986
(Ashley):
Noah, let me see.

51:34.988 --> 51:36.559
What the fuck?!

51:36.561 --> 51:38.528
He doesn't deserve
a cent of Dad's money!

51:38.530 --> 51:40.233
He's just gonna fucking
snort it all away!

51:40.235 --> 51:41.927
Oh, my God!

51:41.929 --> 51:43.401
-She's not wrong.
-(Jared): Yes, she is!

51:43.403 --> 51:45.238
I'm fucking clean, Jared!

51:45.240 --> 51:46.965
(Rachel):
Oh, whatever. It never sticks.

51:47.671 --> 51:49.968
Listen, guys, one less sibling

51:49.970 --> 51:52.212
means more of Dad's money
for the rest of us.

51:52.214 --> 51:54.005
You trying to recruit them
to gang up on me?

51:54.007 --> 51:55.809
No, I know where Jared stands.

51:57.252 --> 52:01.650
Ashley, you do get the severity
of the situation, don't you?

52:01.652 --> 52:05.489
You do get that one of us
is leaving here tonight

52:05.491 --> 52:07.953
in a fucking body bag?

52:08.522 --> 52:11.330
One of our cold dead bodies

52:11.332 --> 52:14.124
is being wheeled out that door

52:14.126 --> 52:17.237
and thrown in the back
of that mobile morgue

52:17.239 --> 52:20.240
at the end of the driveway
right alongside Dad.

52:20.242 --> 52:25.806
Now do you want that dead body
to be your pretty little body?

52:27.414 --> 52:29.546
No, you don't.

52:29.548 --> 52:32.417
Because you have a dream, right?

52:33.052 --> 52:35.288
You're gonna be
a famous actress.

52:35.290 --> 52:37.389
And it'll happen for you, too.

52:37.391 --> 52:39.688
You just gotta keep following
your heart.

52:39.690 --> 52:40.953
As if you care.

52:40.955 --> 52:42.493
You've never even seen
her on stage.

52:42.495 --> 52:43.428
(Rachel): No!

52:44.299 --> 52:45.529
I haven't.

52:46.131 --> 52:49.665
But I do know that following
your heart isn't cheap.

52:52.472 --> 52:54.901
Now, I don't know how big
Dad's estate is,

52:54.903 --> 52:57.607
but think of how much more
of a nest egg you could have

52:57.609 --> 52:59.741
with one of us out
of the picture.

53:02.009 --> 53:03.844
(suspenseful music)

53:04.979 --> 53:07.353
Yeah. Nice try.

53:08.180 --> 53:10.048
But we're stronger than that.

53:20.863 --> 53:23.336
Noah already got
his inheritance.

53:24.867 --> 53:26.471
(Rachel):
What do you mean?

53:26.473 --> 53:29.441
I mean, he's not going to trial.

53:29.976 --> 53:32.378
The woman's family dropped
the charges

53:32.380 --> 53:34.512
because Dad paid them off.

53:35.944 --> 53:38.780
I saw an e-mail
from Dad's lawyers.

53:38.782 --> 53:40.617
He paid them $3,000,000.

53:40.619 --> 53:42.146
-(Jared): Holy shit!
-No, no, no!

53:42.148 --> 53:43.290
I had nothing to do with that!

53:43.292 --> 53:44.753
Dad did that!

53:44.755 --> 53:47.151
I didn't even know about it
until Dawn told me

53:47.153 --> 53:48.757
when she invited me to dinner!

53:48.759 --> 53:50.154
So Dad's estate isn't
being split evenly,

53:50.156 --> 53:51.826
is it? Because you're
already up three mil.

53:51.828 --> 53:53.564
I don't give a shit
about the money!

53:53.566 --> 53:55.368
You guys can have it! Ash!

53:56.195 --> 53:57.403
Ash...

53:57.838 --> 54:00.670
You promised me no more secrets!

54:03.378 --> 54:06.170
(Jared laughs slowly.)
(Noah): Jared, put that back!

54:06.172 --> 54:07.941
Jared, put that back!
What the fuck?!

54:07.943 --> 54:09.514
Huh...

54:09.516 --> 54:11.109
(Jared):
3 million fucking dollars?

54:11.111 --> 54:12.616
Stop! This is fucking crazy!

54:12.618 --> 54:14.178
All of you, stop!

54:14.547 --> 54:15.883
Get the fuck back, Jared!

54:15.885 --> 54:17.555
-Hit him!
-It's not as easy as it looks!

54:17.557 --> 54:19.326
-You fucking hit him!
-(Rachel): I already did!

54:19.328 --> 54:20.855
Just swing, you fucking pussy!

54:20.857 --> 54:21.856
(Noah): Stop! Stop!

54:21.858 --> 54:23.253
Swing!

54:23.255 --> 54:24.793
-Do you want it to be you?
-No!

54:24.795 --> 54:27.026
-We're a fucking family!
-(Rachel): Just fucking swing!

54:27.028 --> 54:29.270
Stop it!
We're a fucking family!

54:33.738 --> 54:35.441
-Fuck this!
-No!

54:36.202 --> 54:38.444
(grunting)

54:43.781 --> 54:45.077
Jared...

54:46.421 --> 54:47.585
Jared...

54:48.280 --> 54:50.753
(breathing heavily)

54:54.022 --> 54:55.461
(clanging)
Agh!

54:56.189 --> 54:57.760
Jesus, fuck!

54:57.762 --> 54:59.256
Ash, please, come on.

54:59.258 --> 55:00.631
(Jared groaning)

55:01.898 --> 55:04.195
Don't do this. Ash, please.

55:04.730 --> 55:06.670
(pepper spray hisses)
(Noah screams in pain)

55:07.574 --> 55:10.036
(indistinct yelling)

55:10.940 --> 55:11.873
(Noah grunts)

55:12.711 --> 55:14.139
(Ashley): Oh!

55:14.141 --> 55:16.416
(grunting)

55:16.418 --> 55:18.649
(tense music)

55:20.488 --> 55:21.718
(stapler clacks)

55:25.460 --> 55:26.855
Hm...

55:27.627 --> 55:28.824
Hm...

55:28.826 --> 55:30.155
(stapler clacks)

55:35.261 --> 55:37.030
So you're a test tube baby?

55:37.032 --> 55:39.131
That because your mom
couldn't mate with a man

55:39.133 --> 55:40.374
without killing him?

55:41.135 --> 55:42.442
No.

55:42.444 --> 55:44.004
My mom said it's because

55:44.006 --> 55:47.172
she didn't want to waste any
of her love on some idiot man.

55:47.174 --> 55:48.910
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

55:48.912 --> 55:50.483
I don't think your mom
is a person

55:50.485 --> 55:52.177
with a whole lot of love
in reserve.

55:55.050 --> 55:57.523
(exhales sharply)
This is a waste.

55:57.525 --> 55:59.151
I have to pee.

55:59.553 --> 56:01.758
Back there, to the right.

56:01.760 --> 56:03.496
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

56:09.636 --> 56:11.768
I don't want you peeing on this.

56:15.873 --> 56:17.378
(sighs)

56:21.043 --> 56:22.746
(Mia sobs quietly)

56:29.249 --> 56:30.985
(radio)
<i> Sir, great news.</i>

56:30.987 --> 56:32.426
<i> We have apprehended Mrs. Kim,</i>

56:32.428 --> 56:33.856
<i> and are en route</i>
<i> to your location.</i>

56:33.858 --> 56:35.220
<i> You can release the Yorks.</i>

56:35.695 --> 56:37.860
<i> ETA 20 minutes.</i>

56:37.862 --> 56:40.126
Uh, no, no, no, no,
no, no... no.

56:40.128 --> 56:44.196
Um... just... bring her
back to headquarters.

56:44.198 --> 56:47.166
(radio):<i> Sir, she says she wants</i>
<i> to do the procedure at home.</i>

56:47.168 --> 56:48.871
Yeah, I don't give a rat's
ass what she wants.

56:48.873 --> 56:50.037
Take her back to headquarters.

56:54.175 --> 56:56.978
(♪♪)

57:01.050 --> 57:02.951
I wiped myself on
your hand towel.

57:03.822 --> 57:05.723
Of course you did.

57:13.293 --> 57:16.063
(sinister music)

57:17.770 --> 57:19.968
(moaning)

57:29.551 --> 57:31.045
(cracking)
Ah!

57:38.252 --> 57:39.460
(tooth clatters)

57:43.290 --> 57:45.961
(breathing heavily)

57:48.229 --> 57:51.604
Close your eyes,
close your eyes...

57:53.575 --> 57:55.806
Picture yourself calm.
(inhales sharply)

57:55.808 --> 57:57.236
Picture yourself calm.

57:57.238 --> 57:58.336
(inhales deeply)

58:01.374 --> 58:03.176
(Grace):
<i> Picture yourself calm.</i>

58:04.410 --> 58:06.652
<i> Picture yourself calm.</i>

58:08.447 --> 58:09.952
Oh, my God.

58:10.592 --> 58:11.888
Grace...

58:12.319 --> 58:13.989
Grace.

58:25.167 --> 58:28.168
(crickets chirping)

58:28.170 --> 58:30.874
(♪♪)

58:34.242 --> 58:35.648
(cell phone thuds)

58:44.483 --> 58:45.955
(Bob): One, two...

58:46.518 --> 58:48.056
One, two...

58:48.630 --> 58:50.025
One, two...

58:50.794 --> 58:53.028
One, two, three,
four, there we go.

58:53.030 --> 58:54.799
Apologies for the counting.

58:54.801 --> 58:56.295
The instructions say it's ready

58:56.297 --> 58:57.703
when you can count to three
between pops.

58:57.705 --> 58:59.166
So that's what I do.

58:59.168 --> 59:00.838
You gotta be careful

59:00.840 --> 59:02.004
'cause the second
you burn one kernel,

59:02.006 --> 59:03.368
the whole bag is ruined.

59:03.370 --> 59:04.875
I don't know why,

59:04.877 --> 59:06.679
but it just tastes off,
you know?

59:06.681 --> 59:10.177
One time, I only...
had four unpopped kernels.

59:10.179 --> 59:11.849
I put a photo of it on Insta.

59:11.851 --> 59:12.718
You should check it out.

59:12.720 --> 59:14.654
I'm @WhatAboutBob42.

59:14.656 --> 59:15.886
Amazing.
I'll do that for sure.

59:15.888 --> 59:16.821
(Bob): Hey!

59:16.823 --> 59:18.218
Don't you want any popcorn?

59:18.220 --> 59:19.593
(Mia):
It's been over an hour.

59:19.595 --> 59:21.353
What are they still
doing in the house?

59:24.666 --> 59:27.491
Well, based on my experience
in similar situations,

59:27.493 --> 59:30.494
I want to say, you know,
killing one another?

59:30.496 --> 59:31.737
(Mia): What?!

59:32.306 --> 59:34.432
No, they're not.
Why would they do that?

59:34.434 --> 59:36.236
Hey, that's not on me.

59:36.238 --> 59:38.535
Your mom came up with that idea
all by herself.

59:38.537 --> 59:40.042
She did not.
She would never do that.

59:40.044 --> 59:41.373
Oh, why?

59:41.375 --> 59:42.748
Because she's such
a good person?

59:42.750 --> 59:44.013
Please.

59:44.015 --> 59:45.212
You know those terrible things

59:45.214 --> 59:46.785
your classmates are saying
about her online

59:46.787 --> 59:48.248
are true, right? Yeah.

59:48.250 --> 59:49.722
Your mom was fully aware

59:49.724 --> 59:51.482
that those pills didn't work,

59:51.484 --> 59:53.220
and yes, she refused
to pull them off the shelf.

59:53.222 --> 59:55.222
So those women got sicker
and sicker because of her!

59:55.224 --> 59:56.487
Stop lying!

59:57.523 --> 59:58.731
(Bob): Tony!

59:59.266 --> 01:00:00.997
-(Tony grunts)
-(thud)

01:00:04.937 --> 01:00:08.136
(sombre music)

01:00:11.372 --> 01:00:12.877
(loud crash)

01:01:02.423 --> 01:01:05.666
(Jared speaking indistinctly
on TV)

01:01:07.263 --> 01:01:10.264
<i> ...our expectation,</i>
<i> our desire</i>

01:01:10.266 --> 01:01:13.399
<i> to achieve victory</i>
<i> on a volunteer basis</i>

01:01:13.401 --> 01:01:15.665
<i> is an abject failure.</i>

01:01:15.667 --> 01:01:17.436
(political commentator
speaking indistinctly)

01:01:30.550 --> 01:01:32.550
(metal clatters to floor)

01:01:35.423 --> 01:01:38.259
(indistinct voices on TV)

01:01:40.494 --> 01:01:43.000
(♪♪)

01:02:50.465 --> 01:02:52.729
Noah.
Please don't.

01:02:52.731 --> 01:02:54.434
What are you doing here?

01:02:54.436 --> 01:02:55.699
(Ashley):
I had to get away.

01:02:55.701 --> 01:02:57.074
I couldn't take it.

01:02:57.076 --> 01:02:58.911
Noah, I'm so sorry.

01:02:58.913 --> 01:03:00.572
I don't know what happened.

01:03:00.574 --> 01:03:02.783
It was Rachel.
She got in my head.

01:03:06.547 --> 01:03:07.788
Where are they?

01:03:08.549 --> 01:03:10.318
They're in the living room.

01:03:10.925 --> 01:03:13.123
They have Dawn's knives.

01:03:14.225 --> 01:03:15.554
I'm gonna go talk to them.

01:03:15.556 --> 01:03:17.259
Did you not just hear
what I said?

01:03:17.261 --> 01:03:18.898
(Noah):
This has to stop.

01:03:18.900 --> 01:03:20.328
Ash...

01:03:21.628 --> 01:03:23.628
it has to stop.

01:03:27.238 --> 01:03:28.534
You stay here.

01:03:28.976 --> 01:03:30.173
No.

01:03:31.275 --> 01:03:33.539
I should go with you.

01:03:33.541 --> 01:03:35.640
They should hear it from
the both of us.

01:03:38.051 --> 01:03:41.646
Get behind me, in case
they gang up on you, too.

01:03:42.748 --> 01:03:43.857
Okay.

01:03:45.058 --> 01:03:46.321
(Noah inhales sharply)

01:03:57.598 --> 01:03:58.905
Hey.

01:04:00.876 --> 01:04:02.436
Look at us.

01:04:04.979 --> 01:04:07.111
You look so happy.

01:04:11.315 --> 01:04:13.249
I'd just started taking piano.

01:04:15.055 --> 01:04:17.550
Nobody called me
a prodigy back then.

01:04:18.894 --> 01:04:20.520
It was still fun.

01:04:23.360 --> 01:04:25.932
And I had a new little sister
to call my own.

01:04:28.728 --> 01:04:30.695
You and me against the world.

01:04:33.733 --> 01:04:36.877
Look at those chubby
little cheeks.

01:04:39.574 --> 01:04:41.442
-Noah...
-(Noah): Yeah?

01:04:42.478 --> 01:04:44.610
-(Rachel grunts)
-(Noah cries out in pain)

01:04:45.382 --> 01:04:47.217
(Jared): Aw! Fuck!

01:04:47.219 --> 01:04:49.384
(indistinct yelling)

01:04:49.386 --> 01:04:51.188
(Jared and Rachel groan loudly)

01:04:52.323 --> 01:04:54.158
Ash, help me!

01:04:54.160 --> 01:04:55.192
Help me!

01:04:55.997 --> 01:04:58.855
-(Ashley): I can't!
-Ash! Ash!

01:04:59.891 --> 01:05:01.726
(grunting)

01:05:03.532 --> 01:05:05.103
Agh!

01:05:06.007 --> 01:05:09.569
(grunting loudly)

01:05:09.571 --> 01:05:10.636
Ah!

01:05:14.642 --> 01:05:16.444
(Rachel):
Open the fucking door!

01:05:17.117 --> 01:05:19.612
(Rachel yells indistinctly)

01:05:20.351 --> 01:05:22.318
(Jared grunts)

01:05:25.257 --> 01:05:26.751
You're fuckin' dead!

01:05:26.753 --> 01:05:28.621
Agh!

01:05:29.261 --> 01:05:30.722
(grunts)
Fuck!

01:05:30.724 --> 01:05:32.064
Die already!

01:05:32.066 --> 01:05:33.593
-(Noah grunts)
-(Rachel): Oh!

01:05:37.335 --> 01:05:38.829
Tell Mia I love her.

01:05:40.437 --> 01:05:41.733
Tell her yourself.

01:05:41.735 --> 01:05:44.538
-(Rachel gasps)
-(thud)

01:05:44.540 --> 01:05:45.902
(fork clatters)

01:05:45.904 --> 01:05:48.410
(Noah breathes heavily)

01:05:48.412 --> 01:05:49.642
Ah!

01:05:50.645 --> 01:05:53.745
(tense music)

01:05:57.289 --> 01:05:59.025
I'm not racist.

01:05:59.660 --> 01:06:02.589
Uh... no, I...
I'm an ally.

01:06:03.097 --> 01:06:04.459
Okay? So, uh...

01:06:04.461 --> 01:06:07.231
you, uh, Mia...

01:06:07.233 --> 01:06:09.332
uh... Dawn...

01:06:09.834 --> 01:06:11.763
I love...
I love you all, okay?

01:06:11.765 --> 01:06:14.073
I... I know you're not
supposed to say,

01:06:14.075 --> 01:06:17.274
"I don't see colour,"
but I don't see colour,

01:06:17.276 --> 01:06:20.739
so none of this has anything
to do with white privilege

01:06:20.741 --> 01:06:22.378
or systemic anything.

01:06:22.380 --> 01:06:24.182
Agh! Ugh!

01:06:26.681 --> 01:06:28.285
Got it, Jared.

01:06:28.587 --> 01:06:29.990
I got it.

01:06:30.982 --> 01:06:32.388
(exhales sharply)

01:06:33.457 --> 01:06:34.753
(Jared coughs)

01:06:37.296 --> 01:06:38.625
(Ashley): Agh!

01:06:39.298 --> 01:06:41.760
Oh! Oh...

01:06:42.499 --> 01:06:45.764
(panting)
Oh, my God.

01:06:46.503 --> 01:06:49.339
Oh! Oh, sh...

01:06:52.971 --> 01:06:55.147
You think I'm the bad guy,
but I'm not.

01:06:55.149 --> 01:06:57.644
I'm only here tonight because
your grandpa invited me.

01:06:57.646 --> 01:06:59.778
He knows I'm doing important
work to save the planet

01:06:59.780 --> 01:07:00.944
for your generation.

01:07:00.946 --> 01:07:02.055
Giving me a fucking break.

01:07:02.057 --> 01:07:03.551
Your generation ruined
the planet.

01:07:03.553 --> 01:07:05.058
Hey, language.

01:07:05.794 --> 01:07:07.621
You need to improve
your outlook, young lady.

01:07:07.623 --> 01:07:09.293
I mean,
I don't think you realize

01:07:09.295 --> 01:07:11.163
how lucky you are to be living
where you do.

01:07:11.165 --> 01:07:13.165
Most of the world now,
it's total anarchy,

01:07:13.167 --> 01:07:14.694
but we still have law and order,

01:07:14.696 --> 01:07:16.366
and we're still
protecting your freedoms.

01:07:16.995 --> 01:07:18.830
Okay. Look.

01:07:20.537 --> 01:07:22.702
You don't understand this
because you're a kid.

01:07:22.704 --> 01:07:23.901
And I get that.

01:07:23.903 --> 01:07:25.903
But when the dust settles,

01:07:25.905 --> 01:07:28.213
when we hit our enlistment goal,

01:07:28.982 --> 01:07:30.875
the great people this country
used to have,

01:07:30.877 --> 01:07:33.911
the really decent,
the righteous people,

01:07:33.913 --> 01:07:35.352
they're gonna be gone.

01:07:35.354 --> 01:07:36.650
Yeah. Whatever.

01:07:36.918 --> 01:07:39.521
(loud slamming)

01:07:39.956 --> 01:07:43.624
No, no, no! Enough with
the fucking attitude!

01:07:44.526 --> 01:07:47.331
After everything I've done,
after everything I've sacrificed

01:07:47.333 --> 01:07:50.026
you damn well better
show me some respect!

01:07:51.469 --> 01:07:53.370
(Tony):
Boss, everything okay in there?

01:07:55.539 --> 01:07:57.836
(Tony knocks on door)
Boss?

01:07:57.838 --> 01:07:59.211
(sniffles)
Yeah, Tony, I'm good!

01:07:59.213 --> 01:08:01.840
It's all good, it's all good,
it's all good...

01:08:04.845 --> 01:08:06.713
Look, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to frighten you.

01:08:06.715 --> 01:08:09.287
I'm just... I know what
I'm talking about. You know?

01:08:09.289 --> 01:08:11.014
I've been inside
these people's homes.

01:08:11.016 --> 01:08:12.851
I've sat with their families.

01:08:12.853 --> 01:08:15.084
And these aren't
the Richie Riches of the world,

01:08:15.086 --> 01:08:17.460
like your kind, with your
massive carbon footprints.

01:08:17.462 --> 01:08:19.759
No, these are... these people
are salt of the earth.

01:08:19.761 --> 01:08:21.794
They've worked hard
their whole lives

01:08:21.796 --> 01:08:23.334
and just couldn't catch a break.

01:08:24.370 --> 01:08:26.733
That is, until the government
offered them a quarter million

01:08:26.735 --> 01:08:28.702
tax-free dollars
to sacrifice themselves,

01:08:28.704 --> 01:08:30.572
and now, they're dying happy

01:08:30.574 --> 01:08:32.068
knowing that their families

01:08:32.070 --> 01:08:33.575
are being taken care of,
you know?

01:08:34.281 --> 01:08:35.907
And that's beautiful.

01:08:42.113 --> 01:08:44.850
My wife Ruth,
she enlisted on Day 14.

01:08:45.886 --> 01:08:47.688
Yeah, she had Parkinson's
for years,

01:08:47.690 --> 01:08:50.625
but we managed, you know,
we managed. It's all good.

01:08:51.127 --> 01:08:53.430
Still, she decided that
since the enlistment program

01:08:53.432 --> 01:08:55.894
didn't give two hoots
about a pre-existing condition,

01:08:55.896 --> 01:08:57.830
she might as well sign up
and get the money

01:08:57.832 --> 01:08:59.931
instead of dying
for nothing, you know?

01:09:02.067 --> 01:09:04.001
Hey, I disagreed.

01:09:04.570 --> 01:09:06.905
But I never won an argument
in all our years of marriage.

01:09:06.907 --> 01:09:08.313
(chuckles)

01:09:10.944 --> 01:09:12.779
Look, I'm sorry that
you're all broken up

01:09:12.781 --> 01:09:14.814
about what's going on
in your grandpa's house,

01:09:14.816 --> 01:09:16.717
but come on, come on!

01:09:17.119 --> 01:09:18.917
Is it so wrong to not want
the new world

01:09:18.919 --> 01:09:21.524
to be filled with terrible
people like your family?

01:09:23.088 --> 01:09:24.329
No.

01:09:25.563 --> 01:09:26.991
I guess not.

01:09:27.626 --> 01:09:29.994
But I don't think
you care about that.

01:09:32.966 --> 01:09:35.439
I just think you like
to watch people die.

01:09:39.071 --> 01:09:40.576
Can't it be both?

01:09:42.008 --> 01:09:46.582
(Jared): Jesus Christ,
this is so fucking bleak.

01:09:46.984 --> 01:09:49.112
I don't know, I...

01:09:49.114 --> 01:09:50.949
Oh, ugh...

01:09:50.951 --> 01:09:54.326
Jesus, is there no way
Bob can just come in here

01:09:54.328 --> 01:09:57.153
and fucking kill him
so we don't have to?

01:09:57.155 --> 01:09:58.363
No, he won't do it.

01:09:58.365 --> 01:09:59.859
No, but he might.

01:09:59.861 --> 01:10:01.399
We could at least ask him.

01:10:01.401 --> 01:10:03.027
It's a waste of time.

01:10:03.329 --> 01:10:06.030
That sadistic fucker is loving
what's happening in here.

01:10:06.032 --> 01:10:08.197
This is what he wanted
all along.

01:10:08.199 --> 01:10:10.738
If we want out,
we have to deliver the body.

01:10:11.674 --> 01:10:14.907
Guys, the way he looked at me
when he realized I betrayed him.

01:10:15.877 --> 01:10:17.811
-I can't...
-(Rachel): Yeah.

01:10:18.979 --> 01:10:20.880
He could've finished me off,
but he didn't.

01:10:20.882 --> 01:10:22.387
Me, too.

01:10:23.753 --> 01:10:25.181
Sorry, Ash, it's okay.

01:10:25.183 --> 01:10:26.985
We're gonna just get this
done real quick.

01:10:26.987 --> 01:10:29.053
It'll be over with
before you know it.

01:10:29.055 --> 01:10:30.890
-On three.
-Yeah, okay, on three.

01:10:31.629 --> 01:10:32.859
Okay.

01:10:33.961 --> 01:10:35.565
-(Ashley): Ugh!
-(Jared): Oh, God.

01:10:35.567 --> 01:10:37.897
-One...
-(Jared): Yeah, one.

01:10:39.736 --> 01:10:41.164
Two...

01:10:41.666 --> 01:10:43.837
-(Jared): Agh...
-(Rachel): Three.

01:10:43.839 --> 01:10:46.037
-(car horn blaring in distance)
-(Jared screams)

01:10:46.039 --> 01:10:47.874
(car horn blaring)

01:10:47.876 --> 01:10:50.580
(Grace): Noah? Noah!

01:10:50.582 --> 01:10:52.076
Noah, please!

01:10:52.078 --> 01:10:53.418
-Who's that?
-Who's that?

01:10:53.820 --> 01:10:56.047
-(horn blaring)
-(Grace): Noah,
are you still here?

01:10:56.049 --> 01:10:57.455
(female guard):
Ma'am, stop right there!

01:10:57.457 --> 01:10:58.918
(Bob): You stay there!

01:11:00.724 --> 01:11:02.889
-(Grace): Noah, where are you?
-(guard): Ma'am!

01:11:03.258 --> 01:11:05.430
Let me go! I don't know
what's going on here,

01:11:05.432 --> 01:11:06.959
but I'm recording everything.

01:11:06.961 --> 01:11:09.192
-Where is Noah?
-Holy shit, that's Grace!

01:11:09.194 --> 01:11:11.260
Oh my God, we're saved.
Grace!

01:11:11.262 --> 01:11:13.196
Hey! Hey, you guys,

01:11:13.198 --> 01:11:15.066
-you're Noah's family, right?
-Yeah.

01:11:15.068 --> 01:11:16.936
(Grace): What's going on here?
Where's Noah?

01:11:16.938 --> 01:11:18.806
Ma'am, I can answer
all your questions.

01:11:18.808 --> 01:11:20.610
I didn't ask you.
I asked them.

01:11:20.612 --> 01:11:21.941
Get back in the house.

01:11:21.943 --> 01:11:24.207
Get them back in the house
right now, come on.

01:11:24.209 --> 01:11:26.451
-Mom!
-Mia!

01:11:26.453 --> 01:11:27.980
(Tony):
Back in the vehicle!

01:11:28.549 --> 01:11:30.950
Ma'am, you're interfering in
official D.O.C.S. business.

01:11:30.952 --> 01:11:32.589
That's a federal offence.

01:11:32.591 --> 01:11:34.085
I thought D.O.C.S.
just euthanized people?

01:11:34.087 --> 01:11:35.592
We've diversified.

01:11:35.594 --> 01:11:37.297
(engine starting)

01:11:38.124 --> 01:11:39.728
Shit!

01:11:41.435 --> 01:11:43.600
Hey! Hey, stop the vehicle!

01:11:43.602 --> 01:11:45.470
-Mom!
-(Rachel): Mia!

01:11:46.165 --> 01:11:47.769
(Bob):
No, no, no, no, no!

01:11:47.771 --> 01:11:49.474
-(Mia): Mm!
-Tony, help me out here.

01:11:49.476 --> 01:11:51.135
Just... careful,
she's a child!

01:11:51.137 --> 01:11:53.104
(Bob):
Be gentle, Tony, gentle.

01:11:54.239 --> 01:11:55.876
Yorks, back in the house!

01:11:55.878 --> 01:11:58.417
-You still owe me a body!
-(Grace): Owe him a body?!

01:11:58.419 --> 01:12:00.650
What is going on here?
Where is Noah?

01:12:00.652 --> 01:12:01.849
Tell me he's alive!

01:12:01.851 --> 01:12:03.180
He is, Grace, he's alive!

01:12:03.182 --> 01:12:04.786
But he needs help!
Please run and get help!

01:12:04.788 --> 01:12:07.250
Okay! Okay!
I'm gonna go get help.

01:12:07.252 --> 01:12:08.691
Just... tell Noah I love him!

01:12:08.693 --> 01:12:09.692
Go, go, run!

01:12:09.694 --> 01:12:10.924
Stop her.

01:12:10.926 --> 01:12:13.795
(tense music)

01:12:15.469 --> 01:12:17.128
-(gunshot)
-(thud)

01:12:21.068 --> 01:12:22.375
(Ashley gasps)

01:12:29.043 --> 01:12:31.648
They killed her.
They fucking killed her!

01:12:31.650 --> 01:12:33.650
She didn't do anything!

01:12:36.787 --> 01:12:38.314
-Oh!
-So, that's it, right?

01:12:38.816 --> 01:12:39.953
You have your second body.

01:12:39.955 --> 01:12:41.427
What, are you kidding me?

01:12:41.429 --> 01:12:43.088
She's not my second body.

01:12:43.090 --> 01:12:45.563
I'm here to collect
two York bodies.

01:12:45.565 --> 01:12:48.500
Now get back inside the house
and finish what you started.

01:12:48.502 --> 01:12:50.502
And don't you dare try
to pin this on me.

01:12:50.504 --> 01:12:52.196
If your family did its part,

01:12:52.198 --> 01:12:53.835
that poor woman would
be alive right now.

01:12:53.837 --> 01:12:56.299
Now get in there.
You've got 15 minutes.

01:13:01.647 --> 01:13:03.240
I meant go get her.

01:13:10.986 --> 01:13:12.920
Don't... don't say anything.

01:13:13.422 --> 01:13:15.989
Let's just go upstairs
and do what we have to do.

01:13:18.158 --> 01:13:20.400
Don't think about it.
Let's just do it.

01:13:20.835 --> 01:13:23.766
I mean, Noah wouldn't want
to be alive right now anyway.

01:13:23.768 --> 01:13:27.770
That woman lying dead out there
was his whole world.

01:13:28.234 --> 01:13:30.410
Yeah... Yeah.

01:13:31.179 --> 01:13:33.908
If you think about it,
we're really doing him a favour.

01:13:34.510 --> 01:13:37.615
I mean... it's fucked up.

01:13:38.409 --> 01:13:40.244
But it's the right thing to do.

01:13:41.148 --> 01:13:43.181
-You know it is.
-Yeah.

01:13:43.183 --> 01:13:44.457
Okay?

01:13:49.464 --> 01:13:50.694
(gasps)

01:13:55.569 --> 01:13:57.228
Noah?

01:14:05.909 --> 01:14:07.073
(Rachel exhales sharply)

01:14:07.878 --> 01:14:09.878
(Jared): Fuck...

01:14:10.375 --> 01:14:11.880
(electrical pop)

01:14:16.623 --> 01:14:18.315
(utensils clattering)

01:14:24.257 --> 01:14:25.762
(Ashley): Noah?

01:14:32.364 --> 01:14:33.539
Noah?

01:14:34.441 --> 01:14:36.740
(Jared): We had nothing to do
with what happened to Grace.

01:14:36.742 --> 01:14:38.104
(Ashley): Noah?

01:14:39.206 --> 01:14:41.811
Come on, Noah,
we don't have much time.

01:14:49.249 --> 01:14:51.150
(Rachel):
We're not mad anymore.

01:14:59.798 --> 01:15:02.161
(Ashley breathing heavily)

01:15:04.638 --> 01:15:07.639
Noah, come on,
you're freaking us out!

01:15:09.137 --> 01:15:12.578
(suspenseful music)

01:15:12.580 --> 01:15:15.372
(Jared): This is bad.
This is so fucking bad.

01:15:34.360 --> 01:15:36.162
Oh, fuck...

01:15:39.134 --> 01:15:40.298
Noah!

01:15:41.499 --> 01:15:43.136
-(knife slices)
-(Ashley grunts)
-(Jared): Oh, my God!

01:15:43.138 --> 01:15:44.467
No, no, no!

01:15:44.469 --> 01:15:45.578
Oh, my God!

01:15:47.747 --> 01:15:49.208
Noah...

01:15:49.210 --> 01:15:51.045
(Noah grunts)

01:15:53.379 --> 01:15:55.247
(Ashley groans)

01:15:58.120 --> 01:16:00.318
(grunting)

01:16:02.454 --> 01:16:05.059
Noah, I'm so sorry.
We're so sorry.

01:16:06.700 --> 01:16:08.029
Agh!

01:16:08.801 --> 01:16:10.768
(Ashley gasps)

01:16:18.206 --> 01:16:21.845
(dramatic music)

01:16:23.343 --> 01:16:24.507
(Ashley shrieks):
No!

01:16:26.511 --> 01:16:27.884
(Noah growls)

01:16:33.925 --> 01:16:35.452
(panting)

01:16:35.454 --> 01:16:36.860
-(Ashley yelps)
-Get off her!

01:16:36.862 --> 01:16:38.554
(Noah): Fuck you!

01:16:38.556 --> 01:16:41.799
If Bob needs a body, it can be
this lying bitch's body.

01:16:41.801 --> 01:16:43.900
(Rachel): Please
just leave her alone.

01:16:45.596 --> 01:16:48.267
(panting)
What would Dad think, huh?

01:16:48.269 --> 01:16:49.675
(Ashley groans)

01:16:49.677 --> 01:16:51.402
(gasping)

01:16:51.404 --> 01:16:53.206
What would Dad think?

01:16:54.715 --> 01:16:56.748
(coughing)

01:16:56.750 --> 01:16:58.409
Huh?

01:16:58.411 --> 01:17:00.686
(Ashley gasps for air)

01:17:06.419 --> 01:17:08.188
Ah!
(groans)

01:17:08.190 --> 01:17:10.960
Don't you fucking
talk about him.

01:17:10.962 --> 01:17:12.390
(shrieking)

01:17:12.392 --> 01:17:15.063
Oh! Oh! Oh!

01:17:16.704 --> 01:17:18.033
Okay! Okay!

01:17:18.035 --> 01:17:19.672
Just leave Ash alone!

01:17:19.674 --> 01:17:21.201
I'm volunteering
for the procedure!

01:17:21.203 --> 01:17:22.334
You don't have to do it!

01:17:22.336 --> 01:17:24.644
You don't have to do it.
I'm volunteering.

01:17:26.846 --> 01:17:29.539
Everything that's happened
tonight is on me.

01:17:30.850 --> 01:17:32.718
You're not the worst of us,
Noah.

01:17:33.380 --> 01:17:34.478
I am.

01:17:35.217 --> 01:17:37.580
I'm cold. I'm selfish.

01:17:37.582 --> 01:17:39.252
(panting)

01:17:39.254 --> 01:17:40.660
So take Mia.

01:17:41.487 --> 01:17:42.662
Please.

01:17:43.863 --> 01:17:46.127
Just take her. Okay?

01:17:46.129 --> 01:17:48.360
(panting)

01:17:48.362 --> 01:17:51.066
You never wanted fame or money.

01:17:51.068 --> 01:17:52.837
You just wanted
a fucking family.

01:17:55.941 --> 01:17:57.600
Just flick the lights.

01:17:57.602 --> 01:17:59.778
-I'm ready, okay?
-(Jared): No, no.

01:17:59.780 --> 01:18:01.472
It should be me.

01:18:01.474 --> 01:18:03.012
'Cause I'm the eldest.

01:18:03.014 --> 01:18:04.981
And I was supposed to look out
for you guys.

01:18:04.983 --> 01:18:07.445
I was always supposed
to look out for you guys

01:18:07.447 --> 01:18:09.854
and I never fucking did.
I'm a really bad brother,

01:18:09.856 --> 01:18:12.615
and I'm a bad husband
and a bad father.

01:18:13.827 --> 01:18:15.486
So if someone...

01:18:15.488 --> 01:18:17.928
is going to have the procedure,
it should be me.

01:18:17.930 --> 01:18:19.457
I have nothing.

01:18:19.459 --> 01:18:21.228
(Ashley): Jared, stop!
You have Lucas!

01:18:23.364 --> 01:18:25.628
He needs you to be here for him.

01:18:26.367 --> 01:18:30.633
No one needs a two-faced
failure.

01:18:30.635 --> 01:18:33.339
If anyone should do
the procedure, it should be me.

01:18:33.341 --> 01:18:34.670
(glass shatters)

01:18:35.706 --> 01:18:37.508
Fuck that!

01:18:40.315 --> 01:18:42.216
No one is volunteering.

01:18:42.885 --> 01:18:45.725
It has to be one of us.
(exhales sharply)

01:18:46.094 --> 01:18:47.826
We have no choice.

01:18:47.828 --> 01:18:49.388
I volunteered first.

01:18:49.723 --> 01:18:52.490
(Noah): No, we've always had
another choice.

01:18:53.801 --> 01:18:55.328
Let's get Bob.

01:18:55.330 --> 01:18:58.199
(Ashley gasps, coughs)

01:19:02.370 --> 01:19:04.403
(Mia):
I need to see my family.

01:19:04.405 --> 01:19:08.407
You'll see them when they blink
the porch lights, not before.

01:19:08.409 --> 01:19:11.575
By then it'll be too late.
(sobbing)

01:19:11.577 --> 01:19:14.248
Someone I love
is gonna die in there.

01:19:14.250 --> 01:19:16.756
Please... please.

01:19:17.825 --> 01:19:20.188
(crying)
Please, Bob, please!

01:19:21.257 --> 01:19:23.829
Please!
(Bob chuckles)

01:19:24.264 --> 01:19:26.260
I need to say goodbye,
at least.

01:19:26.262 --> 01:19:28.900
(screaming):
Let me say goodbye!

01:19:30.002 --> 01:19:32.563
Why?! Why won't you
let me see them?!

01:19:33.032 --> 01:19:35.467
(Noah): A little bit longer,
Ash. Ash, stay with us.

01:19:35.469 --> 01:19:37.502
(Rachel): Fuck, she's losing
a lot of blood.

01:19:37.504 --> 01:19:38.910
(Noah):
Jared, hurry up.

01:19:38.912 --> 01:19:40.472
(Jared):
A few more seconds.

01:19:41.208 --> 01:19:42.848
(Noah): Rach, are you
keeping the pressure?

01:19:42.850 --> 01:19:44.740
(Rachel): Yes, but we need
to do this now.

01:19:46.381 --> 01:19:47.952
-(Noah): Jared?!
-(Jared): Okay, it's ready!

01:19:47.954 --> 01:19:49.250
You got to hold her down,
though.

01:19:49.252 --> 01:19:50.713
(Noah): Ash, Ash...

01:19:51.082 --> 01:19:53.683
Ash, I'm so sorry.
I'm so sorry.

01:19:53.685 --> 01:19:56.895
-I'm so sorry.
-It's not your fault.

01:19:56.897 --> 01:19:59.128
It's supposed to be me and you
against the world,

01:19:59.130 --> 01:20:01.064
and I screwed it up.
Not you, Noah. It was me.

01:20:01.066 --> 01:20:04.694
-Uh, do you want a countdown?
-No! Just fucking do it.

01:20:04.696 --> 01:20:06.597
(Jared): Alright, here we go,
here we go, here we go.

01:20:07.299 --> 01:20:09.567
-(sizzling flesh)
-(Ashley screams in pain)

01:20:15.883 --> 01:20:17.817
(Ashley panting)

01:20:18.985 --> 01:20:21.018
Oh, no, no!
I have to do it again.

01:20:21.020 --> 01:20:24.120
-I'm going again, I'm going--
-(Ashley shrieking)

01:20:34.792 --> 01:20:36.561
(Jared):
Ashley. Ashley...

01:20:36.563 --> 01:20:38.134
Ash, Ash, come on.

01:20:38.136 --> 01:20:39.399
Ashley, Ashley, wake up.

01:20:39.401 --> 01:20:42.204
Wake up, come on.
Ashley!

01:20:50.775 --> 01:20:52.511
(watch beeps)

01:20:52.880 --> 01:20:54.249
Well, time's up.

01:20:54.251 --> 01:20:57.857
One way or another,
we're nearly done here.

01:21:01.357 --> 01:21:03.995
(door opens, shuts)

01:21:03.997 --> 01:21:05.821
(doorbell rings)

01:21:05.823 --> 01:21:07.163
(knocking)

01:21:07.726 --> 01:21:10.298
Hello! Anybody home?

01:21:11.037 --> 01:21:13.070
(door creaks open)

01:21:16.009 --> 01:21:17.239
Huh.

01:21:21.377 --> 01:21:23.113
Not who I expected.

01:21:27.878 --> 01:21:30.351
Where are the rest
of you Yorks at?

01:21:30.353 --> 01:21:32.716
We don't have all night.

01:21:36.524 --> 01:21:37.820
Okay.

01:21:38.493 --> 01:21:40.163
(Tony):
Stop right there.

01:21:41.034 --> 01:21:42.660
Shirts up.

01:21:44.466 --> 01:21:46.202
Turn in a circle.

01:21:47.832 --> 01:21:49.172
Okay.

01:21:49.807 --> 01:21:51.504
Well, whoever's
responsible for this,

01:21:51.506 --> 01:21:53.869
I really appreciate you
saving us the effort

01:21:53.871 --> 01:21:55.706
of bringing
our equipment back in here.

01:21:55.708 --> 01:21:56.806
So, thank you for that.

01:21:56.808 --> 01:21:58.918
Let's get the gurney
in though, Tony.

01:21:59.679 --> 01:22:01.646
(Tony):
All set to go here.

01:22:01.648 --> 01:22:03.087
I guess I owe
you guys some money.

01:22:03.089 --> 01:22:05.056
Now I can split the total
between the three of you,

01:22:05.058 --> 01:22:07.388
but one of you is gonna get
a penny more than the others.

01:22:07.390 --> 01:22:09.720
Some people wouldn't think
that's an issue,

01:22:09.722 --> 01:22:12.063
but some families, they just
fight like crazy over it.

01:22:12.065 --> 01:22:13.427
-(Ashley screams)
-(Tony): Agh!

01:22:13.429 --> 01:22:14.791
Fuck!

01:22:17.334 --> 01:22:19.235
Oh, you bitch! Agh!

01:22:19.237 --> 01:22:20.566
Shut the fuck up!

01:22:22.339 --> 01:22:24.075
Ashley, that was quite
a performance.

01:22:24.877 --> 01:22:27.210
I've seen a lot of dead bodies.
I'm not easily fooled.

01:22:27.212 --> 01:22:28.475
Well done.

01:22:29.049 --> 01:22:30.180
(male guard): Hey!

01:22:31.051 --> 01:22:32.116
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

01:22:32.118 --> 01:22:33.414
(Noah):
Guns down or they're dead!

01:22:33.416 --> 01:22:35.086
(Jared): Do it!

01:22:35.088 --> 01:22:36.879
You don't want to
do this, Yorks.

01:22:36.881 --> 01:22:38.188
We're all bleeding out anyway.

01:22:38.190 --> 01:22:40.190
You tell them to put
their guns down

01:22:40.192 --> 01:22:42.720
-or you'll be joining us.
-(Bob): Put your guns down.

01:22:42.722 --> 01:22:44.293
Do what he fucking says!

01:22:44.889 --> 01:22:46.427
They're not listening.

01:22:47.793 --> 01:22:50.299
They say it's hard to saw
through someone's windpipe, Bob,

01:22:50.301 --> 01:22:52.301
but I bet I could do it
in just one swipe!

01:22:52.303 --> 01:22:53.500
Okay, give 'em your weapons.

01:22:53.502 --> 01:22:54.798
(Bob):
Put your weapons down. Do it.

01:22:54.800 --> 01:22:56.107
Hand over your weapons.

01:22:56.109 --> 01:22:58.472
-Down! Fucking down!
-(Bob): Do what they say!

01:22:58.474 --> 01:23:00.408
(Jared): Give them to me.
Give me your guns.

01:23:00.410 --> 01:23:01.871
Yeah, he's gonna cut
his fuckin' throat.

01:23:01.873 --> 01:23:03.444
-On the ground!
-Listen.

01:23:03.446 --> 01:23:05.512
Hands on your heads,
do as they say.

01:23:06.416 --> 01:23:07.514
Oh.

01:23:07.516 --> 01:23:09.450
(Rachel):
Hands on your head!

01:23:09.452 --> 01:23:11.287
(Bob): Well, if you think
we've never been in a situation

01:23:11.289 --> 01:23:12.915
like this before,
you'd be wrong.

01:23:12.917 --> 01:23:15.159
So let me tell you how
this is gonna play out.

01:23:16.393 --> 01:23:17.557
Ash?

01:23:17.559 --> 01:23:19.361
Ashley!

01:23:20.595 --> 01:23:21.726
(Bob grunts)

01:23:21.728 --> 01:23:23.266
Okay. Alright, I'm good,
let's take 'em--

01:23:23.268 --> 01:23:24.630
Agh!

01:23:29.967 --> 01:23:32.000
(Tony):
Please, I have a wife.

01:23:32.002 --> 01:23:33.441
(Rachel): Shut up.

01:23:33.443 --> 01:23:35.278
(Tony): I have a son, too.
Tony, Jr.

01:23:35.280 --> 01:23:37.940
(Rachel): Cut it out,
or I'm gonna swap you for Bob.

01:23:41.814 --> 01:23:43.286
(Noah): He's awake.

01:23:45.950 --> 01:23:47.455
(Tony):
Boss, I'm sorry.

01:23:47.957 --> 01:23:50.326
They forced me to show them
how to set everything up.

01:23:51.692 --> 01:23:54.264
Tony, Tony, Tony,
Tony, it's okay.

01:23:54.266 --> 01:23:56.431
I've got it all
under control, babe.

01:23:56.433 --> 01:23:58.367
Oh, yeah.

01:23:58.369 --> 01:24:00.171
This is not looking good
for you guys,

01:24:00.173 --> 01:24:03.339
I'm not gonna sugarcoat it.
I'm not gonna sugarcoat it.

01:24:03.341 --> 01:24:05.638
Yeah, this is looking
really bad for us.

01:24:05.640 --> 01:24:07.145
Well, I'm just sayin',

01:24:07.147 --> 01:24:08.641
based on what I'm seeing here,

01:24:08.643 --> 01:24:11.006
not only are all of you
going to jail,

01:24:11.008 --> 01:24:13.217
but the government
now has official custody

01:24:13.219 --> 01:24:15.087
of both Mia and Lucas.

01:24:15.089 --> 01:24:16.484
Excuse me?

01:24:16.486 --> 01:24:18.321
Not me. Not my company.

01:24:18.323 --> 01:24:20.290
We're not in the minor
accommodation business,

01:24:20.292 --> 01:24:21.753
I swear.

01:24:21.755 --> 01:24:24.327
However, if any D.O.C.S.
employee is injured

01:24:24.329 --> 01:24:25.955
in the enactment
of their duties,

01:24:25.957 --> 01:24:27.528
the perpetrators' children

01:24:27.530 --> 01:24:28.925
automatically become wards
of the state.

01:24:28.927 --> 01:24:30.531
It's true. Ask Tony.

01:24:31.402 --> 01:24:32.764
It's true.

01:24:33.173 --> 01:24:34.535
Don't kill me.

01:24:34.537 --> 01:24:36.669
Yeah, you should see
the deplorable conditions

01:24:36.671 --> 01:24:38.176
of these facilities.

01:24:38.178 --> 01:24:40.376
I mean, remember the kids
in cages at the border?

01:24:40.378 --> 01:24:42.312
Yeah. Think that,
but far worse.

01:24:42.314 --> 01:24:44.248
I think you probably want
to keep your fucking hands

01:24:44.250 --> 01:24:45.612
off our kids.

01:24:47.715 --> 01:24:50.980
Then we're screwed no matter
what we do, huh, Bob?

01:24:51.549 --> 01:24:53.554
No reason to leave anyone alive.

01:24:56.229 --> 01:24:59.989
Nugget, gonna have to ask you
to step outside again, okay?

01:25:06.063 --> 01:25:07.931
I'm sorry about your wife.

01:25:08.633 --> 01:25:10.769
It sounded like she was
a really nice person.

01:25:12.839 --> 01:25:16.214
So I doubt the two of you are
gonna end up in the same place.

01:25:23.751 --> 01:25:26.158
Look, I know you're all
very upset,

01:25:26.160 --> 01:25:28.292
I can... I can tell. I...

01:25:28.294 --> 01:25:30.118
It's been a... it's been
a hell of a night, huh?

01:25:30.120 --> 01:25:31.757
(Bob chuckles)

01:25:31.759 --> 01:25:33.957
So, here's what
I'm willing to do.

01:25:35.565 --> 01:25:37.202
Just forget about
this whole situation,

01:25:37.204 --> 01:25:39.028
and me and my men will
just pick up your sister

01:25:39.030 --> 01:25:40.634
off the floor,
and we'll go, okay?

01:25:40.636 --> 01:25:43.340
Deal's a deal.
What do you say?

01:25:56.223 --> 01:25:57.552
Come on.

01:25:57.554 --> 01:26:00.115
That's not Ashley on the floor.

01:26:02.119 --> 01:26:03.756
It isn't?

01:26:03.758 --> 01:26:05.560
Yeah, no, our first attempt
at the procedure

01:26:05.562 --> 01:26:07.331
didn't go too well.

01:26:07.966 --> 01:26:13.095
Tony forgot to tell us to take
the air out of the IV tubes.

01:26:15.000 --> 01:26:18.276
(Noah): You ever see somebody
die of an embolism, Bob?

01:26:18.278 --> 01:26:19.937
It's not quick.

01:26:20.841 --> 01:26:22.874
It's not really fair

01:26:22.876 --> 01:26:25.877
considering that your friend
killed my girlfriend instantly.

01:26:30.983 --> 01:26:34.457
But as my lovely sister
over here put it earlier...

01:26:37.594 --> 01:26:38.824
fuck fair.

01:26:38.826 --> 01:26:40.529
Okay. I can save you all.

01:26:40.531 --> 01:26:41.959
I can save you.

01:26:41.961 --> 01:26:44.126
I can save you
and your children.

01:26:44.128 --> 01:26:46.128
I could've sworn you said
we were all doomed.

01:26:46.130 --> 01:26:48.504
(Bob): No, it's just a matter
of paperwork, that's all.

01:26:48.506 --> 01:26:50.308
I can write something up
to cover for you.

01:26:50.310 --> 01:26:52.640
You can cover us for murdering
a D.O.C.S. agent?

01:26:52.642 --> 01:26:55.346
Yeah, I'll just say your father
reacted violently

01:26:55.348 --> 01:26:57.348
when his wife departed,

01:26:57.350 --> 01:26:59.317
and took us by surprise.
That's actually happened.

01:26:59.319 --> 01:27:00.549
My bosses will believe that.

01:27:00.551 --> 01:27:02.111
Then when he calmed down,

01:27:02.113 --> 01:27:03.552
he decided to go ahead
with the procedure

01:27:03.554 --> 01:27:05.015
for his children's sake.

01:27:05.017 --> 01:27:06.852
That part is true.
It's so true.

01:27:06.854 --> 01:27:08.656
Alright, no, please.

01:27:08.658 --> 01:27:09.690
Okay. Wait, wait.

01:27:09.692 --> 01:27:11.527
What about Dawn?
What about Dawn?

01:27:12.365 --> 01:27:13.694
What about her?

01:27:14.367 --> 01:27:15.861
We have her at headquarters.

01:27:16.363 --> 01:27:18.193
Yeah, yeah, we have her--

01:27:18.195 --> 01:27:19.634
Agh!

01:27:24.938 --> 01:27:27.510
(Bob choking)

01:27:29.349 --> 01:27:31.514
-(Bob coughing)
-I don't know shit about that.

01:27:32.880 --> 01:27:34.649
Look, I'll bring Dawn
back to you.

01:27:34.651 --> 01:27:36.420
She doesn't have to have
the procedure.

01:27:36.422 --> 01:27:37.850
Your family has given up enough.

01:27:37.852 --> 01:27:40.149
Please don't push that.
Please don't push that.

01:27:40.151 --> 01:27:41.821
You'll never see her
alive again.

01:27:41.823 --> 01:27:43.251
They'll kill her
and it'll be on you.

01:27:43.253 --> 01:27:44.659
It'll be all on you.
Come on!

01:27:44.661 --> 01:27:46.760
Hold on, hold on...
Come on!

01:27:46.762 --> 01:27:48.861
What don't you people
understand?

01:27:48.863 --> 01:27:50.225
Huh? What... what?

01:27:50.227 --> 01:27:52.194
There's a worldwide crisis
going on

01:27:52.196 --> 01:27:53.932
and I'm doing important work!

01:27:53.934 --> 01:27:55.868
And you, you, you...

01:27:55.870 --> 01:27:57.804
you're just pieces
of human excrement

01:27:57.806 --> 01:27:59.641
polluting the planet
with your every breath!

01:28:02.008 --> 01:28:03.876
I don't deserve to die!

01:28:04.417 --> 01:28:05.944
You deserve to die!

01:28:06.584 --> 01:28:08.683
Not me! You!

01:28:09.356 --> 01:28:11.246
(silence)

01:28:14.625 --> 01:28:17.659
(piano playing)

01:29:21.956 --> 01:29:24.286
(TV announcer):
<i>Week 40's Enlisters of the Week</i>

01:29:24.288 --> 01:29:26.530
<i> are Grace Dawson</i>
<i> and Ashley York.</i>

01:29:26.532 --> 01:29:28.730
<i> Friends for years,</i>
<i> the inseparable pair</i>

01:29:28.732 --> 01:29:30.864
<i> told our D.O.C.S.</i>
<i> procedure practitioner</i>

01:29:30.866 --> 01:29:32.800
<i> that they chose</i>
<i> to enlist together</i>

01:29:32.802 --> 01:29:35.902
<i> so they could inspire others</i>
<i> to do everything they could do</i>

01:29:35.904 --> 01:29:38.366
<i>to help heal our ailing planet.</i>

01:29:38.368 --> 01:29:40.203
It was a beautiful procedure.

01:29:40.205 --> 01:29:42.579
It ranked right up there
with the best of them.

01:29:43.281 --> 01:29:44.614
(TV announcer):
<i> Grace and Ashley,</i>

01:29:44.616 --> 01:29:46.649
<i> a grateful nation thanks you.</i>

01:29:52.052 --> 01:29:54.184
(♪♪)
